D("resonate",{etymology:E("From Latin resonare, re- ‘again’ + sonare ‘sound’; the verb describes both a ringing echo and an idea that feels meaningful to an audience.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resonate"),contexts:[C("resonate.s1","心理","The account of losing a first job resonated with readers who had faced the same setback.","关于失去第一份工作的讲述引起了同样遭遇挫折的读者共鸣。","Resonate with readers means feel meaningful or familiar to them.","Resonated with names the audience; the who-clause identifies their shared experience.","Readers connect personally with the story rather than literally hearing an echo."),C("resonate.s2","聲學","The singer stopped, but her last note continued to resonate inside the stone hall.","歌手停下后，最后一个音仍在石厅里回响。","Resonate can mean produce a sound that continues after the source stops.","But contrasts the stopped singer with the lingering note.","This is the literal acoustic sense.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The singer's final note resonate through the empty hall.","The singer's final note resonates through the empty hall.","The singular subject note takes resonates in the present tense.")],quiz:[Q("resonate.q1","resonate.s1","meaning","A story resonates with a listener when it ___.",["feels personally meaningful","is printed in tiny type","is measured only in decibels"],"feels personally meaningful","This is the figurative connection sense.","meaning"),Q("resonate.q2","resonate.s2","context","A bell continues to resonate after being struck. What happens?",["Its sound rings on","Its metal turns liquid","Its handle gets shorter"],"Its sound rings on","The acoustic sense is a continuing or echoing sound.","context"),Q("resonate.q3","resonate.s1","collocation","The proposal resonated ____ local residents.",["with","at","under"],"with","Resonate with an audience is the usual construction.","collocation"),Q("resonate.q4","resonate.s2","meaning","Which scene shows literal resonance?",["A drumbeat echoing in a tunnel","A slogan matching voters' values","A plan seeming fair to workers"],"A drumbeat echoing in a tunnel","The tunnel echo is an acoustic event.","meaning")]});
D("resonator",{etymology:E("Formed from resonate with the instrument/agent suffix -or; resonate continues Latin resonare, ‘sound again’.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resonator"),contexts:[C("resonator.s1","物理","The violin's hollow wooden body acts as a resonator, strengthening string vibrations into audible sound.","小提琴中空的木制琴身起共鸣器作用，把琴弦的振动增强为可听见的声音。","A resonator vibrates at particular frequencies and reinforces a signal.","Acts as connects the body to its function; the participial phrase gives the result.","The body reinforces vibrations; it is not the string itself.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The padded violin case is its resonator because it absorbs every vibration and prevents sound.","The hollow violin body is its resonator because it reinforces the strings' vibrations.","A resonator reinforces selected vibrations; an absorbing case is not serving that role.")],quiz:[Q("resonator.q1","resonator.s1","meaning","What does a resonator do in an acoustic instrument?",["Reinforces vibrations at particular frequencies","Records the musician's name","Removes every sound from a room"],"Reinforces vibrations at particular frequencies","A resonator strengthens a frequency-specific signal.","meaning"),Q("resonator.q2","resonator.s1","context","Which item acts as a resonator?",["A hollow guitar body amplifying string vibration","A cloth bag holding guitar picks","A label showing the guitar's price"],"A hollow guitar body amplifying string vibration","The body reinforces the strings' sound.","context"),Q("resonator.q3","resonator.s1","word-formation","Here the suffix -or most naturally marks ___.",["an object performing a function","a place where someone sleeps","a quality described by an adjective"],"an object performing a function","-or can form an instrument or agent noun.","word-formation"),Q("resonator.q4","resonator.s1","meaning","A circuit resonator is designed to respond strongly at ___.",["particular frequencies","every temperature equally","the hour on a clock"],"particular frequencies","The source sense specifies particular frequencies.","meaning")]});
D("resort",{etymology:E("From Old French resortir, ‘go out again, return’, from re- ‘again’ + sortir ‘go out’; the noun came to mean a place or means people turn to.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resort"),contexts:[C("resort.s1","旅遊","Families booked a lakeside resort where children could swim and adults could rest.","几家人预订了湖畔度假村，孩子可以游泳，大人可以休息。","A resort is a place people visit for a holiday.","Where introduces facilities; booked a resort identifies the destination.","The noun names a holiday destination.") ,C("resort.s2","應急","After every cheaper repair failed, the museum resorted to borrowing a climate-control unit.","所有更便宜的维修方案都失败后，博物馆只得借用一台温控设备。","To resort to something is to use it when better options are unavailable.","Resorted to takes a noun or gerund; after marks failed alternatives.","Borrowing was the last available measure.") ,C("resort.s3","書面","Legal action remained the tenant's last resort after repeated repair requests were ignored.","多次要求维修均遭忽视后，诉诸法律仍是租户最后的办法。","A resort can be a means one turns to for help.","Last modifies resort; the after-clause explains why it is needed.","This means an option, not a holiday place.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","When cheaper options failed, the clinic resorted borrowing a generator.","When cheaper options failed, the clinic resorted to borrowing a generator.","Resort takes to before a noun or -ing complement.")],quiz:[Q("resort.q1","resort.s1","meaning","A mountain resort is primarily ___.",["a holiday destination","a survey participant","a sound-measuring circuit"],"a holiday destination","The first sense is a place visited on holiday.","meaning"),Q("resort.q2","resort.s2","grammar","After the pumps failed, the farm resorted ____ a temporary well.",["to digging","digging","for dig"],"to digging","Resort to is followed by a noun or gerund.","grammar"),Q("resort.q3","resort.s3","context","Calling a lawyer is a last resort when it is ___.",["the final means used after other options fail","a seaside holiday place","the routine first step"],"the final means used after other options fail","A resort may be a means one turns to.","context"),Q("resort.q4","resort.s1","word-choice","The family spent a week at a beach ____.",["resort","resound","respondent"],"resort","A beach resort is a holiday destination.","word-choice")]});
D("resound",{etymology:E("From Old French resoner and Latin resonare, re- ‘again’ + sonare ‘sound’; it can describe a loud echo or widespread acclaim.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resound"),contexts:[C("resound.s1","聲學","The cannon's report resounded across the valley and startled sheep on the far slope.","炮声在山谷间回响，惊动了远处山坡上的羊。","Resound means make a loud sound that carries or echoes.","Across the valley marks the sound's reach; and joins its result.","The sound is physically loud and travels far.") ,C("resound.s2","成就","Her name resounded throughout the scientific community after the team published its breakthrough.","团队发表突破性成果后，她的名字在科学界广为传颂。","Resound can mean become widely known because of success.","After gives the cause; throughout marks the breadth of recognition.","This figurative sense concerns reputation rather than audible echo.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The cannon's report resound through the valley every morning.","The cannon's report resounds through the valley every morning.","The singular subject report takes the -s form resounds.")],quiz:[Q("resound.q1","resound.s1","meaning","If a bell resounds through a hall, its sound ___.",["is loud and carries through the space","is hidden from every listener","turns into written text"],"is loud and carries through the space","The literal sense is a loud sound that carries.","meaning"),Q("resound.q2","resound.s2","context","A scientist's name resounds after a discovery when the scientist ___.",["becomes widely known for the achievement","moves away from a ringing bell","stops speaking to colleagues"],"becomes widely known for the achievement","This is the figurative fame sense.","context"),Q("resound.q3","resound.s1","grammar","Choose the correct sentence about one bell.",["The bell resounds across the square.","The bell resound across the square.","The bell are resound across the square."],"The bell resounds across the square.","A singular present-tense subject takes resounds.","grammar"),Q("resound.q4","resound.s2","meaning","Which sentence uses resound figuratively?",["Her victory resounded throughout the league.","A drum resounded in the warehouse.","Thunder resounded over the lake."],"Her victory resounded throughout the league.","This describes widespread recognition of a success.","meaning")]});
D("resource",{etymology:E("Via Old French ressource from resourdre, ‘rise again’, ultimately Latin resurgere, re- ‘again’ + surgere ‘rise’; it came to mean a supply or means available for use.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resource"),contexts:[C("resource.s1","教育","The school shared its online resources so pupils without textbooks could still complete the science project.","学校共享了在线资源，让没有课本的学生也能完成科学项目。","A resource is a supply of materials or other things that can be used.","So introduces the purpose; without textbooks identifies the need met.","The materials are available inputs for the project.") ,C("resource.s2","性格","With the bus cancelled and no taxi available, Jo showed great resource by arranging a lift with a farmer.","公交取消又叫不到出租车，Jo 灵机应变，安排农夫顺路送她。","Resource can mean the ability to find clever ways around difficulty.","With sets the problem; by introduces Jo's solution.","This tests inventiveness rather than a material supply.")],mistakes:[M("countability","The library bought three useful resource for the history class.","The library bought three useful resources for the history class.","When resource means a countable source, three requires plural resources.")],quiz:[Q("resource.q1","resource.s1","meaning","A clean-water resource is ___.",["a supply people can use","a feeling of admiration","a reply to a question"],"a supply people can use","The first sense is a usable supply.","meaning"),Q("resource.q2","resource.s2","context","Someone shows resource when a plan fails and they ___.",["find a clever practical alternative","wait without considering options","count chairs in the room"],"find a clever practical alternative","This is the ingenuity sense.","context"),Q("resource.q3","resource.s1","plural","The team used several community ____ to plan the event.",["resources","resourcefulness","resourced"],"resources","Several takes the plural count noun resources.","plural"),Q("resource.q4","resource.s2","meaning","Which phrase uses resource to mean ingenuity?",["a person of great resource","a mineral resource underground","a list of course resources"],"a person of great resource","This use means practical inventiveness.","meaning")]});
D("resourceful",{etymology:E("From resource + -ful, the adjective-forming suffix meaning ‘full of’ or ‘characterized by’; resource entered English through Old French ressource.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resourceful"),contexts:[C("resourceful.s1","救援","The resourceful hikers used a foil blanket to signal a rescue helicopter after their phone lost power.","手机没电后，有办法的徒步者用铝箔毯向救援直升机发信号。","Resourceful describes someone who solves problems cleverly with available means.","Used ... to signals the improvised tool and purpose; after gives the obstacle.","They adapt equipment rather than waiting helplessly.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","A resourceful mechanic gave up when one wrench was missing and refused to try another tool.","A resourceful mechanic improvised with another tool when the first wrench was missing.","Resourceful implies practical ingenuity when the expected tool is unavailable.")],quiz:[Q("resourceful.q1","resourceful.s1","meaning","A resourceful cook facing an almost empty pantry is likely to ___.",["combine the few ingredients creatively","insist that no meal is possible","throw away every pot"],"combine the few ingredients creatively","Resourceful people find solutions with limited means.","meaning"),Q("resourceful.q2","resourceful.s1","context","Which action shows resourcefulness after a bicycle tire goes flat far from home?",["Use a repair kit to patch the tube","Leave the bicycle in the road","Wait for the tire to inflate itself"],"Use a repair kit to patch the tube","The rider makes use of available tools to solve the problem.","context"),Q("resourceful.q3","resourceful.s1","word-formation","In resourceful, -ful contributes the sense ___.",["characterized by or full of a quality","without a quality","the state of being a quality"],"characterized by or full of a quality","-ful forms an adjective meaning full of or characterized by.","word-formation"),Q("resourceful.q4","resourceful.s1","collocation","The resourceful crew found a way ____ the broken winch.",["around","with","under"],"around","Find a way around a problem means devise an alternative.","collocation")]});
D("resourcefulness",{etymology:E("From resourceful + -ness, a suffix that forms a noun for a quality or state; resourceful is resource + -ful.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resourcefulness"),contexts:[C("resourcefulness.s1","野外","The team's resourcefulness kept camp warm: when the stove broke, they insulated the tent with dry leaves.","炉子坏了，队员用干树叶给帐篷隔热；他们的机敏让营地保持温暖。","Resourcefulness is skill at finding solutions with limited means.","The colon introduces evidence; when marks the obstacle prompting it.","The improvised insulation demonstrates the quality.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","Her resourcefulness meant she owned a warehouse full of spare equipment.","Her ample resources meant she owned a warehouse full of spare equipment.","Resourcefulness is ingenuity; resources are supplies or assets.")],quiz:[Q("resourcefulness.q1","resourcefulness.s1","meaning","A rescue team's resourcefulness is its ability to ___.",["solve problems with limited equipment","store a large quantity of fuel","follow a map without thinking"],"solve problems with limited equipment","Resourcefulness is practical problem-solving ability.","meaning"),Q("resourcefulness.q2","resourcefulness.s1","context","Which detail demonstrates an engineer's resourcefulness?",["She makes a temporary clamp from spare wire","She orders a standard replacement part","She lists tools in a catalogue"],"She makes a temporary clamp from spare wire","Improvising a workable fix shows resourcefulness.","context"),Q("resourcefulness.q3","resourcefulness.s1","word-formation","The suffix -ness in resourcefulness turns an adjective into ___.",["a noun naming a quality","a past-tense verb","an adverb of manner"],"a noun naming a quality","-ness commonly forms a noun for a state or quality.","word-formation"),Q("resourcefulness.q4","resourcefulness.s1","confusable","Which phrase names clever problem-solving rather than supplies?",["the crew's resourcefulness","the crew's fuel resources","the crew's financial resources"],"the crew's resourcefulness","Resourcefulness is ingenuity; resources are supplies.","confusable")]});
D("resources",{etymology:E("Plural of resource, from Old French ressource, ultimately Latin resurgere ‘rise again’; today it commonly means usable supplies, people, time, or assets.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resource"),contexts:[C("resources.s1","公益","The clinic pooled its staff and transport resources to deliver medicine to villages cut off by floods.","诊所整合人员和交通资源，把药品送到被洪水阻隔的村庄。","Resources are people, materials, time, or supplies available for a goal.","Pooled takes resources as its object; to deliver states the goal.","Staff and vehicles are inputs the clinic can deploy.") ,C("resources.s2","財務","After the merger, the small firm had enough financial resources to open a second office.","合并后，这家小公司有足够的财力开设第二间办公室。","Resources can mean money and assets available to an organization.","Enough is followed by an infinitive describing the affordable action.","Here the phrase means available capital and assets.")],mistakes:[M("plural","The department's resources is spread across three regional offices.","The department's resources are spread across three regional offices.","Resources is plural, so it takes are.")],quiz:[Q("resources.q1","resources.s1","meaning","In a relief operation, staff, trucks, and medicine are ___.",["resources","responses","retirements"],"resources","They are supplies and people available for the relief goal.","meaning"),Q("resources.q2","resources.s2","context","A firm with limited financial resources has limited ___.",["money and assets available to spend","staff members' memories","public respect"],"money and assets available to spend","Financial resources are available funds and assets.","context"),Q("resources.q3","resources.s1","grammar","Choose the verb for the plural subject resources.",["The resources are ready.","The resources is ready.","The resources has ready."],"The resources are ready.","Resources takes a plural verb.","grammar"),Q("resources.q4","resources.s1","word-choice","The rescue team used its ____ carefully: fuel, radios, and trained staff.",["resources","resourceful","respondent"],"resources","These supplies and people are resources.","word-choice")]});
D("respect",{etymology:E("From Latin respectus ‘regard, consideration’, past participle of respicere ‘look back at’, re- ‘back’ + specere ‘look’; the sense broadened to esteem and due regard.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respect"),contexts:[C("respect.s1","職場","The apprentice earned respect by admitting the measurement error and correcting the report before anyone relied on it.","学徒承认测量错误，并在报告被人采信前更正，因此赢得了敬重。","Respect is admiration or esteem for someone's qualities.","By introduces what earned respect; before marks the timely correction.","Others regard the apprentice highly for honesty.") ,C("respect.s2","社區","Please respect the residents' request to keep the lane clear after 8 p.m.","请尊重居民晚上八点后保持巷道畅通的要求。","As a verb, respect means treat a wish or rule as important and comply.","Request is the object; the infinitive states the requested action.","Here respect means observe a request.") ,C("respect.s3","比較","The two designs differ in one important respect: only the newer one can be repaired locally.","两种设计有一个重要方面不同：只有较新的那种能在当地维修。","A respect can mean a particular feature or dimension of comparison.","In one respect introduces the dimension; the colon identifies it.","This countable noun means an aspect.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The students have respect at their teacher for explaining the proof.","The students have respect for their teacher for explaining the proof.","The idiom is respect for someone, not respect at someone.")],quiz:[Q("respect.q1","respect.s1","meaning","A nurse earns respect when colleagues ___.",["admire her skill and integrity","list her name alphabetically","ask her to leave"],"admire her skill and integrity","Respect as a noun is esteem based on qualities.","meaning"),Q("respect.q2","respect.s2","context","To respect a quiet-hours rule means to ___.",["observe it and avoid making noise","say it is printed neatly","compare it with a map"],"observe it and avoid making noise","The verb means comply with or honor the rule.","context"),Q("respect.q3","respect.s3","meaning","In 'the plans differ in one respect', respect means ___.",["a particular feature or aspect","admiration for a person","a polite greeting"],"a particular feature or aspect","The phrase identifies one dimension of comparison.","meaning"),Q("respect.q4","respect.s1","collocation","Trainees have great ____ for the experienced pilot.",["respect","respective","respectively"],"respect","Have respect for is the standard collocation.","collocation")]});
D("respectable",{etymology:E("From respect + -able, via French respectable; the suffix means ‘worthy of’ or ‘capable of’, and the adjective describes decent conduct or fairly good size/quality.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respectable"),contexts:[C("respectable.s1","社會","Although he was poor, the shopkeeper remained respectable: he dealt honestly with every customer.","尽管贫穷，这名店主仍然品行端正：他诚实对待每位顾客。","Respectable can describe conduct most people consider morally acceptable.","Although contrasts poverty with conduct; the colon gives evidence.","The adjective evaluates the shopkeeper's behavior.") ,C("respectable.s2","商業","The local bakery earned a respectable profit in its first year, enough to pay staff and replace the oven.","当地面包店第一年获得相当可观的利润，足以支付工资并更换烤箱。","Respectable can mean fairly large or good in quality.","Enough to gives a concrete measure of the profit's adequacy.","Here the word means reasonably good, not morally decent.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The auditor called the forged invoices respectable because they were dishonest and illegal.","The auditor called the forged invoices disreputable because they were dishonest and illegal.","Respectable means morally acceptable; dishonest illegal invoices are not respectable.")],quiz:[Q("respectable.q1","respectable.s1","meaning","A respectable witness is generally seen as ___.",["morally acceptable","extremely noisy","financially bankrupt by definition"],"morally acceptable","This is the conduct-related sense.","meaning"),Q("respectable.q2","respectable.s2","context","A shop made a respectable profit. The profit was ___.",["fairly good in size","too small to pay any rent","a person giving a reference"],"fairly good in size","Respectable can mean fairly large or good.","context"),Q("respectable.q3","respectable.s1","word-choice","The charity's ____ record persuaded donors that funds were handled honestly.",["respectable","respectively","respect"],"respectable","The adjective describes morally acceptable conduct.","word-choice"),Q("respectable.q4","respectable.s2","meaning","Which means 'quite good' rather than 'morally decent'?",["a respectable attendance at the concert","a respectable judge who follows the law","a respectable neighbor who keeps promises"],"a respectable attendance at the concert","Attendance is judged fairly good in size.","meaning")]});
D("respected",{etymology:E("Past participle and adjective from respect, borrowed through French from Latin respectus ‘regard, consideration’.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respected"),contexts:[C("respected.s1","學術","The respected botanist corrected her published table when a new specimen disproved one measurement.","新标本推翻一项测量后，这位受人尊敬的植物学家更正了已发表的表格。","Respected means held in esteem for achievement, character, or position.","When gives the reason for the correction; respected modifies botanist.","Her reputation rests on expertise and intellectual honesty.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The respected surgeon have trained two generations of nurses.","The respected surgeon has trained two generations of nurses.","The singular subject surgeon takes has, not have.")],quiz:[Q("respected.q1","respected.s1","meaning","A respected judge is one whom people ___.",["hold in esteem for sound work or character","have formally retired from office","use as a unit of distance"],"hold in esteem for sound work or character","Respected describes someone held in high regard.","meaning"),Q("respected.q2","respected.s1","context","Who is most likely a respected mentor?",["A patient teacher trusted by former students","A stranger whose advice is always ignored","A visitor who has not met the group"],"A patient teacher trusted by former students","Trust and regard support the adjective.","context"),Q("respected.q3","respected.s1","grammar","Choose the correct sentence.",["The respected editor has corrected the record.","The respected editor have corrected the record.","The respected editor are corrected the record."],"The respected editor has corrected the record.","The singular subject editor agrees with has.","grammar"),Q("respected.q4","respected.s1","meaning","The respected scientist's standing comes from ___.",["the esteem others have for her work","the quantity of lab equipment alone","the volume of her voice"],"the esteem others have for her work","The adjective concerns regard earned through qualities or achievement.","meaning")]});
D("respective",{etymology:E("From Medieval Latin respectivus, from respectus ‘regard’; the adjective marks things considered separately in relation to each member of a group.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respective"),contexts:[C("respective.s1","教育","After the ceremony, graduates returned to their respective classrooms to collect projects they had left there.","典礼后，毕业生各自回到自己的教室，取走留在那里的项目。","Respective means separate and belonging to each person in a group.","Their respective classrooms distributes one room to each graduate.","The adjective signals separate ownership, not a shared room.") ,C("respective.s2","體育","The two runners and their respective coaches stood together for the team photograph.","两名跑者和各自的教练一起拍了队伍合照。","Respective can pair each member of one group with a corresponding member of another.","Their respective coaches maps each runner to that runner's coach.","The groups correspond member by member.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The twins put their respective coats into one shared locker, meaning the coats belonged jointly to both.","The twins put their coats into one shared locker; respective would mean each coat belonged separately to one twin.","Respective marks separate one-to-one belonging, not joint ownership.")],quiz:[Q("respective.q1","respective.s1","meaning","The workers returned to their respective desks means they ___.",["each went to the desk assigned to them","all went to one desk together","returned to desks chosen for someone else"],"each went to the desk assigned to them","Respective distributes ownership separately across a group.","meaning"),Q("respective.q2","respective.s2","context","The players and their respective trainers are paired how?",["Each player with that player's own trainer","All players with one unrelated trainer","Each trainer with a different stadium"],"Each player with that player's own trainer","The adjective marks corresponding pairs.","context"),Q("respective.q3","respective.s1","grammar","Choose the natural phrase for separate assignments.",["the students' respective lockers","the students' respective locker when each has a different one","the students respectively locker"],"the students' respective lockers","Respective is an adjective modifying lockers; respectively is an adverb.","grammar"),Q("respective.q4","respective.s1","meaning","What does respective add in 'authors signed their respective chapters'?",["Each author signed the chapter belonging to that author","Both authors signed one chapter together","The chapters were signed alphabetically"],"Each author signed the chapter belonging to that author","The adjective maps each person to a separate item.","meaning")]});
D("respectively",{etymology:E("From respective + adverb-forming -ly; respective derives from Medieval Latin respectivus, ‘having regard to each separately’.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respectively"),contexts:[C("respectively.s1","數據","The north and south sensors recorded 18 and 23 degrees, respectively.","北部与南部传感器分别记录了18度和23度。","Respectively assigns each item in one list to the item in the same position in another.","The adverb follows the paired values; list order determines the mapping.","North pairs with 18 and south with 23, in that order.") ,C("respectively.s2","工作","The two clerks handled the applications respectively, each taking a separate half of the queue.","两名办事员分别处理申请，各自负责队列的一半。","Respectively can emphasize that members act separately, not together.","Each taking clarifies the separate division of work.","This sense stresses separate action.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The north and south stations recorded 18 and 23 degrees respectively, but the report pairs north with 23 and south with 18.","The north and south stations recorded 18 and 23 degrees, respectively, pairing north with 18 and south with 23.","Respectively preserves the stated order of the lists; reversing the pairings is incorrect.")],quiz:[Q("respectively.q1","respectively.s1","meaning","If Ana and Bo scored 8 and 6 respectively, who scored 8?",["Ana","Bo","Both scored 8"],"Ana","Respectively pairs the first name with the first score.","meaning"),Q("respectively.q2","respectively.s2","context","Two nurses respectively covered the morning and evening shifts. What does this suggest?",["Each covered a different shift","They both covered both shifts together","No shift was assigned"],"Each covered a different shift","This sense emphasizes separate assignments.","context"),Q("respectively.q3","respectively.s1","grammar","Choose the punctuated sentence.",["The ports are 400 and 700 km away, respectively.","The ports are 400 and 700 km away respectively; respectively.","The ports respectively, are 400 and 700 km away, respectively,"],"The ports are 400 and 700 km away, respectively.","A comma commonly sets off respectively at the end of a paired list.","grammar"),Q("respectively.q4","respectively.s1","meaning","First and second trial dates were May and June, respectively. When was trial two?",["June","May","Both dates"],"June","The second item pairs with the second date.","meaning")]});
D("respiration",{etymology:E("From Latin respiratio, from respirare ‘breathe again’, re- ‘again’ + spirare ‘breathe’; English uses it for breathing and cellular energy release.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respiration"),contexts:[C("respiration.s1","醫療","The paramedic checked the injured cyclist's respiration while a colleague prepared an oxygen mask.","同事准备氧气面罩时，急救员检查了受伤骑车者的呼吸。","Respiration is the process of breathing air in and out.","While marks simultaneous actions; respiration is the object of checked.","The paramedic is assessing breathing.") ,C("respiration.s2","生物","In the experiment, yeast continued cellular respiration after the lights were switched off.","实验中，即使灯关掉后，酵母仍继续进行细胞呼吸。","Cellular respiration is the chemical process in cells that releases energy.","After marks that the process continues despite darkness.","This is the cell-level chemical sense, not simply breathing.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The biologist called air moving into the lungs cellular respiration, although no cell chemistry was being discussed.","The biologist called air moving into the lungs breathing; cellular respiration names the energy-releasing process inside cells.","Respiration can mean breathing, but cellular respiration specifically names cell chemistry.")],quiz:[Q("respiration.q1","respiration.s1","meaning","A nurse monitors a patient's respiration to check ___.",["the patient's breathing","the patient's yearly income","the patient's handwriting"],"the patient's breathing","This is the bodily breathing sense.","meaning"),Q("respiration.q2","respiration.s2","context","Cellular respiration is studied to learn how cells ___.",["release usable energy through chemical reactions","move air through a nose","make an echo in a room"],"release usable energy through chemical reactions","The cellular sense concerns energy release.","context"),Q("respiration.q3","respiration.s1","collocation","The doctor counted the patient's rate of ____.",["respiration","respectively","retirement"],"respiration","Rate of respiration is a standard medical phrase for breathing rate.","collocation"),Q("respiration.q4","respiration.s2","meaning","Which phrase names the chemical process in cells?",["cellular respiration","artificial respiration","shallow respiration"],"cellular respiration","Cellular identifies the intracellular process.","meaning")]});
D("respiratory",{etymology:E("From Latin respiratorius, from respirare ‘breathe’; the adjective relates to respiration and the organs or process of breathing.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respiratory"),contexts:[C("respiratory.s1","醫療","The doctor ordered a chest scan after the patient developed a persistent respiratory infection.","患者出现持续性呼吸道感染后，医生安排了胸部扫描。","Respiratory means connected with breathing or the breathing system.","After marks the symptom leading to the scan; respiratory modifies infection.","The infection affects the system used for breathing.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","A broken ankle was treated as a respiratory injury because it made walking painful.","A broken ankle was treated as a musculoskeletal injury because it affected bone and movement.","Respiratory concerns breathing; a broken ankle affects the musculoskeletal system.")],quiz:[Q("respiratory.q1","respiratory.s1","meaning","A respiratory therapist primarily works with ___.",["breathing and the lungs","legal contracts","river navigation"],"breathing and the lungs","Respiratory relates to the breathing system.","meaning"),Q("respiratory.q2","respiratory.s1","context","Which case involves a respiratory symptom?",["A patient struggles to breathe","A patient misplaces a passport","A patient forgets a melody"],"A patient struggles to breathe","Breathing difficulty concerns the respiratory system.","context"),Q("respiratory.q3","respiratory.s1","collocation","The lungs and airways form part of the ____ system.",["respiratory","respective","resonator"],"respiratory","Respiratory system is the standard collocation.","collocation"),Q("respiratory.q4","respiratory.s1","meaning","A respiratory illness affects a person's ability to ___.",["breathe","retire","respect a rule"],"breathe","The adjective pertains to breathing.","meaning")]});
D("respire",{etymology:E("From Latin respirare, re- ‘again’ + spirare ‘breathe’; it means breathe, and in biology also describes cellular gas exchange.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respire"),contexts:[C("respire.s1","生物","The researcher sealed the chamber to measure how rapidly the seeds respire while germinating.","研究人员密封了腔室，以测量种子发芽时呼吸的速度。","Respire means take in and release air or, of cells, exchange gases.","To measure gives the purpose; while marks ongoing germination.","The verb describes biological gas exchange.")],mistakes:[M("word form","A human can respire, but the sentence 'She respire slowly' is grammatically correct.","A human can respire, but the sentence should read 'She respires slowly.'","With singular she, the present-tense verb needs the third-person -s ending.")],quiz:[Q("respire.q1","respire.s1","meaning","In biology, living cells respire when they ___.",["exchange gases as part of their life processes","write a spoken reply","withdraw from a sports match"],"exchange gases as part of their life processes","Respire is the biological verb for breathing or gas exchange.","meaning"),Q("respire.q2","respire.s1","context","Which statement uses respire naturally?",["The germinating seed respires as it uses stored energy.","The seed respires the letter to its owner.","The seed respires the referee after the match."],"The germinating seed respires as it uses stored energy.","Seeds respire during germination.","context"),Q("respire.q3","respire.s1","grammar","The small animal ____ through its skin.",["respires","respire","respires to"],"respires","A singular subject takes respires.","grammar"),Q("respire.q4","respire.s1","meaning","Respire is closest in meaning to ___.",["breathe or exchange gases","admire a quality","return to a holiday place"],"breathe or exchange gases","Respire names breathing or biological gas exchange.","meaning")]});
D("respond",{etymology:E("From Latin respondere ‘answer, promise in return’, re- ‘back’ + spondere ‘promise’; English uses it for replies and reactions.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respond"),contexts:[C("respond.s1","溝通","Please respond to the editor's question by noon so the article can be revised before publication.","请在中午前答复编辑的问题，以便文章能在发表前修订。","Respond means give an answer orally or in writing.","To the editor's question specifies what is answered; so introduces the purpose.","The reply is directed to a question.") ,C("respond.s2","醫療","The patient's fever began to respond to treatment after the antibiotic dose was adjusted.","调整抗生素剂量后，患者的发烧开始对治疗产生反应。","Respond can mean react to a treatment or situation.","Respond to treatment names the stimulus; after gives when improvement began.","The condition changes in reaction to treatment.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The patient responded the new antibiotic with a lower fever.","The patient responded to the new antibiotic with a lower fever.","Respond takes to before the stimulus or treatment.")],quiz:[Q("respond.q1","respond.s1","meaning","If a manager responds to an email, the manager ___.",["sends an answer","changes the office temperature","withdraws from a race"],"sends an answer","This is the reply sense.","meaning"),Q("respond.q2","respond.s2","context","A tumor responds to a drug when it ___.",["shows a change because of the treatment","writes a letter to the doctor","moves to another hospital by itself"],"shows a change because of the treatment","Respond has a reaction-to-treatment sense.","context"),Q("respond.q3","respond.s1","collocation","The witness responded ____ the lawyer's question.",["to","for","at"],"to","Respond to a question is the standard construction.","collocation"),Q("respond.q4","respond.s2","meaning","Which sentence means 'react' rather than 'answer'?",["The crop responded well to extra water.","She responded to the email with a note.","He responded to the greeting politely."],"The crop responded well to extra water.","The crop changes in reaction to water.","meaning")]});
D("respondent",{etymology:E("From Latin respondent-, the present participle stem of respondere ‘answer’; the noun names someone who answers, especially in a survey or legal case.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/respondent"),contexts:[C("respondent.s1","調查","Each respondent could skip the household-income question without losing access to the rest of the survey.","每位受访者都可以跳过家庭收入问题，而不影响填写其余问卷。","A respondent is a person who answers survey questions.","Each distributes the option across participants; without marks that skipping does not affect access.","This person is answering a survey.") ,C("respondent.s2","法律","In the appeal, the respondent argued that the lower court had applied the statute correctly.","在上诉案中，被上诉方主张下级法院正确适用了该法规。","A respondent is the party who answers a legal appeal or proceeding.","In the appeal gives the setting; that-clause states the argument.","This is the legal party sense.") ,C("respondent.s3","法律","The respondent party filed its written reply before the hearing.","应诉方在听证会前提交了书面答辩。","As an adjective, respondent means answering or replying.","Respondent modifies party and describes its role.","Here it is adjectival, not a noun for a survey participant.")],mistakes:[M("plural","The survey respondent were asked to estimate their weekly travel time.","The survey respondents were asked to estimate their weekly travel time.","Were requires a plural subject; respondents is the plural form.")],quiz:[Q("respondent.q1","respondent.s1","meaning","A respondent in an opinion poll is ___.",["someone who answers the survey","the person who writes every question","a device measuring rainfall"],"someone who answers the survey","The survey sense names a participant who answers.","meaning"),Q("respondent.q2","respondent.s2","context","In a court appeal, the respondent is the party who ___.",["answers the appeal","conducts a street survey","records the courtroom temperature"],"answers the appeal","The legal sense is the responding party.","context"),Q("respondent.q3","respondent.s3","grammar","In 'the respondent party filed a reply,' respondent modifies ___.",["party","filed","reply"],"party","Respondent is an adjective describing the party's role.","grammar"),Q("respondent.q4","respondent.s1","plural","Several survey ____ completed the form.",["respondents","respondent","respondent's"],"respondents","Several requires the plural respondents.","plural")]});
D("response",{etymology:E("From Old French respons and Latin responsum, the neuter past participle of respondere ‘answer’; it names a reply or reaction.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/response"),contexts:[C("response.s1","健康","The patient showed a rapid response to the new dose, with the swelling decreasing by the next morning.","患者对新剂量迅速产生反应，次日早晨肿胀便减轻了。","A response is a change caused by something else.","With states the observed change; the with-clause gives evidence.","This is the reaction sense.") ,C("response.s2","溝通","We received a written response to the complaint two days after submitting it.","提交投诉两天后，我们收到了书面答复。","A response is an answer given by letter, speech, or action.","To the complaint identifies the matter answered; after gives when it arrived.","This is the reply sense.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","We received a response of our complaint from the council.","We received a response to our complaint from the council.","The usual construction is a response to a question, request, or complaint.")],quiz:[Q("response.q1","response.s1","meaning","A plant's response to drought might be ___.",["its leaves curling as the soil dries","a letter it sends to the farmer","a list of survey participants"],"its leaves curling as the soil dries","A response can be a change caused by conditions.","meaning"),Q("response.q2","response.s2","context","A written response to an invitation is ___.",["a reply saying whether the person will attend","a change in body temperature","a list of office supplies"],"a reply saying whether the person will attend","This is the answer sense.","context"),Q("response.q3","response.s2","collocation","The company issued a response ____ the safety complaint.",["to","on","at"],"to","Response to is the correct preposition.","collocation"),Q("response.q4","response.s1","meaning","Which is a biological response rather than a verbal reply?",["The seedling bends toward the light.","The clerk answers the letter.","The witness says yes."],"The seedling bends toward the light.","A plant's movement is a reaction to its environment.","meaning")]});
D("responsibility",{etymology:E("From responsible + -ity, via French responsabilité; responsible traces to Latin respondere ‘answer for’, so the noun can mean duty or accountability.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/responsibility"),contexts:[C("responsibility.s1","職場","One responsibility of the lab manager is to train new staff to dispose of samples safely.","实验室经理的一项职责是培训新员工安全处置样本。","Responsibility is a duty or task someone is required to perform.","One responsibility is followed by an of-phrase naming the task; to train explains it.","This sense is assigned work, not blame.") ,C("responsibility.s2","事故","The contractor accepted responsibility for the damaged water pipe and paid for its repair.","承包商承认对水管损坏负有责任，并支付了维修费用。","Responsibility can mean blame or accountability for an event.","Accepted responsibility for names the accountable party and damage.","The contractor takes ownership of causing the damage.") ,C("responsibility.s3","治理","Public officials have a responsibility to explain how public money is spent.","公职人员有责任说明公共资金的使用方式。","Responsibility can be a duty to explain actions and accept scrutiny.","To explain gives the obligation; how-clause specifies what must be explained.","This is accountability to the public.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The contractor accepted responsibility of the cracked pipe and arranged its repair.","The contractor accepted responsibility for the cracked pipe and arranged its repair.","Accept responsibility for an outcome uses for, not of.")],quiz:[Q("responsibility.q1","responsibility.s1","meaning","A nurse's responsibility on a night shift may be ___.",["checking patients' medication records","being admired by every visitor","answering a poll"],"checking patients' medication records","A responsibility is an assigned duty.","meaning"),Q("responsibility.q2","responsibility.s2","context","A company accepts responsibility for a spill when it ___.",["admits accountability for causing or handling it","says the spill was pleasant","asks customers to fill in a poll"],"admits accountability for causing or handling it","This is the blame/accountability sense.","context"),Q("responsibility.q3","responsibility.s3","collocation","An elected official has a responsibility ____ explain public decisions.",["to","at","for to"],"to","Have a responsibility to do something is standard.","collocation"),Q("responsibility.q4","responsibility.s1","meaning","Which example names a duty rather than blame?",["It is my responsibility to lock the archive.","The firm accepted responsibility for the leak.","The driver denied responsibility for the crash."],"It is my responsibility to lock the archive.","Locking the archive is a task the speaker must perform.","meaning")]});
