D("responsible",{etymology:E("From Old French responsable, from Latin respons- (the stem of respondere, ‘answer for’) + -ible; it describes duty, causation, or trustworthy conduct.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/responsible"),contexts:[C("responsible.s1","行政","Nora is responsible for checking every permit's address before it is approved.","Nora 负责在许可证获批前核对每张许可证上的地址。","Responsible for means having the duty of dealing with something.","For introduces the assigned task; the before-clause sets its timing.","This is the duty sense.") ,C("responsible.s2","事故","Investigators found that a faulty valve was responsible for the pressure loss.","调查人员发现，故障阀门是压力损失的原因。","Responsible for can mean being the cause of an outcome.","That introduces the finding; for links the valve to the loss.","The valve caused the problem.") ,C("responsible.s3","信任","Only a responsible adult may collect the children from the school office.","只有可靠的成年人可以从学校办公室接走孩子。","Responsible can mean sensible and trustworthy.","Responsible modifies adult; only limits collection to trusted people.","This sense describes dependable character.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The caretaker is responsible of locking the museum at night.","The caretaker is responsible for locking the museum at night.","Responsible takes for before a duty or cause.")],quiz:[Q("responsible.q1","responsible.s1","meaning","If Mei is responsible for payroll, she ___.",["has the duty of handling payroll","caused every employee to resign","answered a public opinion poll"],"has the duty of handling payroll","This is the duty sense.","meaning"),Q("responsible.q2","responsible.s2","context","The storm was responsible for the delay means it ___.",["caused the delay","was assigned to count tickets","admired the passengers"],"caused the delay","Responsible for can identify a cause.","context"),Q("responsible.q3","responsible.s3","meaning","A responsible babysitter is expected to be ___.",["sensible and trustworthy","unwilling to answer any question","the direct cause of a storm"],"sensible and trustworthy","This is the character sense.","meaning"),Q("responsible.q4","responsible.s1","collocation","Who is responsible ____ updating the emergency contact list?",["for","to","at"],"for","Responsible for is standard when naming a duty.","collocation")]});
D("responsive",{etymology:E("From respond + -ive, via French responsive; respond comes from Latin respondere ‘answer’, and the adjective describes quick reaction or a favorable treatment effect.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/responsive"),contexts:[C("responsive.s1","科技","The new map app is responsive to a finger tap, redrawing the route almost immediately.","这款新地图应用能迅速响应手指轻点，几乎立即重新绘制路线。","Responsive means reacting quickly and effectively.","Responsive to names the stimulus; the participial phrase shows the quick result.","The interface reacts without a noticeable delay.") ,C("responsive.s2","醫療","The infection was responsive to the first course of antibiotics, so the fever soon fell.","感染对第一疗程抗生素有良好反应，因此发烧很快退了。","A condition is responsive to treatment when the treatment has a good effect.","Responsive to identifies the medicine; so connects the improvement.","This is the favorable-treatment sense.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The infection was responsive of the prescribed medicine and the fever fell.","The infection was responsive to the prescribed medicine and the fever fell.","Responsive takes to before the stimulus or treatment.")],quiz:[Q("responsive.q1","responsive.s1","meaning","A responsive website ___.",["reacts quickly to user input","rejects every click","prints a paper map"],"reacts quickly to user input","The first sense is quick positive reaction.","meaning"),Q("responsive.q2","responsive.s2","context","If a patient's illness is responsive to a drug, the drug ___.",["has a beneficial effect on it","has not been tested","is used only to label a bottle"],"has a beneficial effect on it","This is the treatment-effect sense.","context"),Q("responsive.q3","responsive.s1","collocation","The dashboard is responsive ____ touch commands.",["to","on","from"],"to","Responsive to introduces what the system reacts to.","collocation"),Q("responsive.q4","responsive.s2","meaning","Which use refers to a treatment working well?",["The tumor was responsive to therapy.","The keyboard was responsive to a tap.","The clerk was responsive to the email."],"The tumor was responsive to therapy.","The medical condition improves with treatment.","meaning")]});
D("responsiveness",{etymology:E("From responsive + -ness, the suffix forming a noun for a quality; responsive derives from respond, ultimately Latin respondere ‘answer’.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/responsiveness"),contexts:[C("responsiveness.s1","服務","Customers praised the repair desk's responsiveness because it returned calls within an hour.","顾客称赞维修台响应迅速，因为它一小时内就回电。","Responsiveness is the quality of reacting promptly and helpfully.","Because introduces evidence; it returned states how quickly staff responded.","The noun describes quick service.") ,C("responsiveness.s2","治理","The councillor's responsiveness to residents' concerns improved after weekly public meetings began.","每周公开会议开始后，议员回应居民关切的态度有所改善。","Responsiveness can mean willingness to listen and give helpful answers.","To residents' concerns specifies the people and issues addressed.","This is willingness to engage, not merely speed.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The help desk's responsiveness have improved since it began replying the same day.","The help desk's responsiveness has improved since it began replying the same day.","Responsiveness is a singular uncountable noun and takes has.")],quiz:[Q("responsiveness.q1","responsiveness.s1","meaning","A service desk with high responsiveness ___.",["answers requests promptly and helpfully","keeps every request unanswered","is made only of spare parts"],"answers requests promptly and helpfully","Responsiveness is the quality of reacting quickly and well.","meaning"),Q("responsiveness.q2","responsiveness.s2","context","A mayor shows responsiveness to residents by ___.",["listening to concerns and giving useful replies","canceling every public meeting","publishing an unrelated weather chart"],"listening to concerns and giving useful replies","The second sense stresses willingness to listen and respond.","context"),Q("responsiveness.q3","responsiveness.s1","word-formation","The suffix -ness in responsiveness makes ___.",["a noun for a quality","a past-tense verb","a comparative adjective"],"a noun for a quality","-ness derives a noun from the adjective responsive.","word-formation"),Q("responsiveness.q4","responsiveness.s1","grammar","Choose the sentence with correct agreement.",["The team's responsiveness has improved.","The team's responsiveness have improved.","The team's responsiveness are improved."],"The team's responsiveness has improved.","Responsiveness is singular and takes has.","grammar")]});
D("rest",{etymology:E("From Old English rest, of Germanic origin; the noun denotes a pause or what remains, while the verb can mean relax, lie, or be supported.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/rest"),contexts:[C("rest.s1","健康","After the overnight shift, Lina took a short rest before driving home.","上完夜班后，Lina 短暂休息了一会儿才开车回家。","A rest is a period of relaxation or sleep.","After places the pause between work and driving.","This is a break from activity.") ,C("rest.s2","健康","The injured bird rested beneath a hedge until the wildlife carer arrived.","受伤的小鸟在树篱下歇着，直到野生动物护理员到来。","As a verb, rest means stop activity and relax.","Until marks how long the bird remained still.","The bird is inactive while recovering.") ,C("rest.s3","分配","Mina packed half the rice for lunch and saved the rest for tomorrow.","Mina 把一半米饭装作午餐，把剩下的留到明天。","The rest means the part left after some has been used or removed.","Half contrasts with the rest; for tomorrow gives its later use.","Here rest is a remaining portion.") ,C("rest.s4","論證","The appeal rests on a witness who saw the vehicle leave the site.","这项上诉依据一位目击车辆离开现场的证人。","To rest on a fact means be based on or depend on it.","On introduces the supporting basis; who-clause identifies the witness.","This is the figurative basis sense.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The appeal rests at a single witness who saw the vehicle leave.","The appeal rests on a single witness who saw the vehicle leave.","The basis sense uses rest on, not rest at.")],quiz:[Q("rest.q1","rest.s1","meaning","Taking a rest after a long walk means ___.",["pausing to relax","continuing to sprint","selling the walking shoes"],"pausing to relax","A rest is a period of inactivity or relaxation.","meaning"),Q("rest.q2","rest.s3","context","If a baker uses three of ten eggs and saves the rest, how many are saved?",["seven","three","ten"],"seven","The rest is what remains after three are used.","context"),Q("rest.q3","rest.s4","meaning","If a case rests on new evidence, the case ___.",["depends on that evidence","is physically lying on paper","has been forgotten"],"depends on that evidence","Rest on can mean be based on.","meaning"),Q("rest.q4","rest.s2","grammar","Choose the correct past-tense sentence.",["The dog rested by the gate.","The dog rest by the gate yesterday.","The dog resting by the gate yesterday."],"The dog rested by the gate.","The regular past tense is rested.","grammar")]});
D("rest on",{etymology:E("A phrasal verb formed from rest (Old English rest) + on; the preposition develops the sense of a claim or decision being supported by a basis.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/rest"),contexts:[C("rest on.s1","法律","The verdict may rest on whether the camera timestamp is accurate.","判决可能取决于摄像头时间戳是否准确。","To rest on something is to depend on it for a decision or truth.","Whether introduces the uncertain point that controls the verdict.","The outcome depends on the timestamp's accuracy.") ,C("rest on.s2","物理","A narrow beam rests on two stone pillars, which carry its weight.","一根窄梁架在两根石柱上，由它们承重。","Rest on can mean be placed on something and supported by it.","On introduces the supporting pillars; which-clause describes their function.","This is the literal support sense.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The verdict rests in whether the witness saw the car.","The verdict rests on whether the witness saw the car.","The idiom is rest on a fact or whether-clause.")],quiz:[Q("rest on.q1","rest on.s1","meaning","A decision that rests on a medical test ___.",["depends on the test result","is physically balanced on a test tube","has already been canceled"],"depends on the test result","This is the figurative dependency sense.","meaning"),Q("rest on.q2","rest on.s2","context","A shelf rests on brackets when the brackets ___.",["support its weight","write its instructions","measure its length"],"support its weight","This is the literal support sense.","context"),Q("rest on.q3","rest on.s1","collocation","The case may rest ____ the final DNA result.",["on","at","under"],"on","Rest on introduces a supporting basis.","collocation"),Q("rest on.q4","rest on.s2","meaning","Which sentence uses literal physical support?",["The statue rests on a granite base.","The plan rests on public trust.","The outcome rests on one vote."],"The statue rests on a granite base.","The statue is physically supported by the base.","meaning")]});
D("restart",{etymology:E("From re- ‘again’ + start, an English formation for starting again after a pause or interruption.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restart"),contexts:[C("restart.s1","科技","After installing the update, the technician restarted the server so the new security rules would load.","安装更新后，技术员重新启动服务器，让新的安全规则载入。","Restart means start something again.","After gives the preceding event; so introduces the purpose.","The server begins another operating cycle.")],mistakes:[M("verb-form","After the update, the technician restart the server to load the changes.","After the update, the technician restarted the server to load the changes.","A completed past action needs restarted, not the base form restart.")],quiz:[Q("restart.q1","restart.s1","meaning","To restart a frozen computer is to ___.",["start it again","remove its screen","turn it into a printer"],"start it again","Restart means begin again after an interruption.","meaning"),Q("restart.q2","restart.s1","context","The band paused after a power cut, then restarted the concert. What did it do?",["began the performance again","canceled every future concert","replaced the audience"],"began the performance again","The performance resumed from an interruption.","context"),Q("restart.q3","restart.s1","word-formation","The prefix re- in restart contributes the meaning ___.",["again","before","against"],"again","Re- commonly means again in this formation.","word-formation"),Q("restart.q4","restart.s1","grammar","Choose the sentence with the correct past form.",["We restarted the router at noon.","We restart the router at noon yesterday.","We restarting the router at noon."],"We restarted the router at noon.","Restarted is the simple past form.","grammar")]});
D("restate",{etymology:E("Formed from re- ‘again’ + state, from Latin status ‘standing, condition’; it means say or express something again, often more clearly.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restate"),contexts:[C("restate.s1","溝通","When the witness looked confused, the lawyer restated the question in simpler words.","证人显得困惑时，律师用更简单的话重述了问题。","Restate means express the same point again, often in a clearer form.","When marks the reason; in simpler words describes the new wording.","The lawyer changes the phrasing without changing the issue.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The chairperson restate the motion before the vote yesterday.","The chairperson restated the motion before the vote yesterday.","A completed past action takes restated.")],quiz:[Q("restate.q1","restate.s1","meaning","If a teacher restates an instruction, the teacher ___.",["expresses it again, perhaps more clearly","withdraws it permanently","asks a survey respondent to leave"],"expresses it again, perhaps more clearly","Restate means say or express again.","meaning"),Q("restate.q2","restate.s1","context","A speaker restates a complicated point in plain language to ___.",["make the same idea easier to understand","introduce an unrelated argument","avoid answering forever"],"make the same idea easier to understand","Restating can clarify without changing the point.","context"),Q("restate.q3","restate.s1","word-formation","In restate, re- means ___.",["again","under","away"],"again","The prefix signals doing the stating again.","word-formation"),Q("restate.q4","restate.s1","grammar","Choose the correct sentence.",["She restated her concern at the meeting.","She restate her concern yesterday.","She restating her concern yesterday."],"She restated her concern at the meeting.","Restated is the correct past form.","grammar")]});
D("restatement",{etymology:E("From restate + -ment, a noun-forming suffix; restate combines re- ‘again’ with state ‘express’.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restatement"),contexts:[C("restatement.s1","財務","The auditor requested a restatement of the annual accounts after finding an error in reported revenue.","发现报告收入有误后，审计员要求重述年度账目。","A restatement is a statement or set of figures expressed again in corrected form.","Of the annual accounts identifies what is restated; after gives the reason.","The figures are issued again because the original report was wrong.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The company's restatement of its earnings were issued on Friday.","The company's restatement of its earnings was issued on Friday.","The singular noun restatement takes was.")],quiz:[Q("restatement.q1","restatement.s1","meaning","A restatement of accounts is ___.",["a revised presentation of previously reported figures","a prediction made before any accounts exist","a list of employees' vacation dates"],"a revised presentation of previously reported figures","Restatement means stating figures again, often to correct them.","meaning"),Q("restatement.q2","restatement.s1","context","A newspaper prints a restatement after correcting a false figure. It has ___.",["reissued the information in corrected form","deleted every unrelated page","changed the paper's size"],"reissued the information in corrected form","The corrected statement replaces the earlier one.","context"),Q("restatement.q3","restatement.s1","word-formation","The suffix -ment in restatement forms ___.",["a noun for a result or act","a comparative adjective","a present-tense verb"],"a noun for a result or act","-ment makes a noun from restate.","word-formation"),Q("restatement.q4","restatement.s1","grammar","Choose the correct agreement.",["The restatement was published.","The restatement were published.","The restatement are published yesterday."],"The restatement was published.","Restatement is a singular noun.","grammar")]});
