D("restlessness",{etymology:E("From restless + -ness, the noun-forming suffix for a state or quality; restless is rest + -less.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restlessness"),contexts:[C("restlessness.s1","健康","Her restlessness kept her awake: she changed position every few minutes and could not settle.","她因焦躁而难以入睡：每隔几分钟就换姿势，怎么也安定不下来。","Restlessness is an inability to relax or stay still.","The colon gives observable signs; every few minutes marks repetition.","The noun names the unsettled state.") ,C("restlessness.s1","生活","A growing restlessness with routine led him to apply for a field assignment.","对日常生活越来越不耐烦，使他申请了外勤职位。","Restlessness can be dissatisfaction that creates a desire for change.","With routine identifies what he is tired of; led to gives the result.","This is the figurative dissatisfaction sense.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The restlessness of the toddlers were obvious during the long wait.","The restlessness of the toddlers was obvious during the long wait.","Restlessness is a singular uncountable noun and takes was.")],quiz:[Q("restlessness.q1","restlessness.s1","meaning","Visible restlessness in a waiting room might include ___.",["pacing and repeated position changes","quietly sleeping for hours","reading one page without moving"],"pacing and repeated position changes","This is physical inability to settle.","meaning"),Q("restlessness.q2","restlessness.s1","context","A person's restlessness with routine may lead them to ___.",["seek a new kind of work","request the same task forever","avoid all change they want"],"seek a new kind of work","Figurative restlessness is dissatisfaction with the current pattern.","context"),Q("restlessness.q3","restlessness.s1","word-formation","The ending -ness in restlessness forms ___.",["a noun naming a state","an adverb of manner","a past participle"],"a noun naming a state","-ness turns restless into a quality or state noun.","word-formation"),Q("restlessness.q4","restlessness.s1","grammar","Choose the correct agreement.",["The restlessness was difficult to ignore.","The restlessness were difficult to ignore.","The restlessness are difficult to ignore yesterday."],"The restlessness was difficult to ignore.","The abstract noun restlessness is singular.","grammar")]});
D("restoration",{etymology:E("From restore + -ation, via French restauration and Latin restauratio, from restaurare ‘renew, rebuild’; the noun names the act or result of returning something to an earlier condition.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restoration"),contexts:[C("restoration.s1","文物","The restoration of the painted ceiling took two years because conservators removed each layer of soot by hand.","彩绘天花板的修复耗时两年，因为修复人员逐层手工清除烟灰。","Restoration is the process of returning an object to a former condition.","Of the painted ceiling identifies the object; because explains the duration.","The work repairs and recovers an older appearance.") ,C("restoration.s2","政治","The restoration of the elected council followed the end of military rule.","军事统治结束后，民选委员会得以恢复。","Restoration can mean the return of a previous system or authority.","Of identifies what was brought back; followed marks the sequence.","The council resumes its former position.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The restoration of the old bridge were completed before winter.","The restoration of the old bridge was completed before winter.","The singular noun restoration takes was.")],quiz:[Q("restoration.q1","restoration.s1","meaning","A painting's restoration is ___.",["work returning it toward an earlier condition","the act of selling every brush","a forecast of next year's weather"],"work returning it toward an earlier condition","The first sense is repair and recovery of an object's condition.","meaning"),Q("restoration.q2","restoration.s2","context","The restoration of a parliament means ___.",["bringing a former political body back","cleaning soot from a ceiling","replacing a restaurant menu"],"bringing a former political body back","Restoration can be the return of a system or institution.","context"),Q("restoration.q3","restoration.s1","word-formation","The suffix -ation in restoration forms ___.",["a noun for an act or process","a comparative adverb","a plural verb"],"a noun for an act or process","-ation forms process or result nouns from verbs.","word-formation"),Q("restoration.q4","restoration.s1","grammar","Choose the correct sentence.",["The restoration was completed in June.","The restoration were completed in June.","The restoration are completed last June."],"The restoration was completed in June.","Restoration is singular and takes was.","grammar")]});
D("restore",{etymology:E("From Old French restorer and Latin restaurare ‘renew, rebuild’; it means return something to an earlier, sound, or usable condition.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restore"),contexts:[C("restore.s1","修復","Volunteers restored the flood-damaged footbridge with new boards while preserving its original stone supports.","志愿者用新木板修复了被洪水损坏的人行桥，同时保留原有石墩。","Restore means return something to a former or usable condition.","With introduces the repair materials; while contrasts repair with preservation.","The bridge is made usable again.") ,C("restore.s2","健康","A quiet afternoon restored her energy after the overnight journey.","经过一夜旅程后，一个安静的下午让她恢复了精力。","Restore can mean bring back a previous condition or feeling.","After gives the depleted state that preceded recovery.","Her energy returns.") ,C("restore.s3","法律","The court ordered the landlord to restore the deposit that had been wrongly withheld.","法院命令房东退还被不当扣留的押金。","Restore can mean give back property or money to its rightful owner.","That-clause identifies the deposit and its prior withholding.","This is restitution of something taken away.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The court restored the deposit by keeping it permanently and refusing to return it to the tenant.","The court returned the deposit to the tenant after it had been wrongly withheld.","To restore money in this sense is to give it back; keeping it is the opposite.")],quiz:[Q("restore.q1","restore.s1","meaning","To restore a damaged chair is to ___.",["repair it so it returns to usable condition","break it into smaller pieces","move it to a different room unchanged"],"repair it so it returns to usable condition","Restore means return an object to an earlier or sound condition.","meaning"),Q("restore.q2","restore.s2","context","A night's sleep restored the runner's energy when the runner ___.",["felt energetic again","lost all strength permanently","was given a new pair of shoes"],"felt energetic again","This is the return-to-a-condition sense.","context"),Q("restore.q3","restore.s3","meaning","If a court orders a payment restored, it orders that the money be ___.",["given back to the person entitled to it","destroyed","counted but withheld"],"given back to the person entitled to it","This sense is to return property or money.","meaning"),Q("restore.q4","restore.s1","grammar","Choose the correct past-tense sentence.",["Workers restored the footbridge.","Workers restore the footbridge yesterday.","Workers restoring the footbridge yesterday."],"Workers restored the footbridge.","The regular past form is restored.","grammar")]});
D("restrain",{etymology:E("From Old French restreindre and Latin restringere, re- ‘back’ + stringere ‘bind tight’; it means hold back, control, or prevent movement.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restrain"),contexts:[C("restrain.s1","安全","The handler restrained the excited dog with a lead until the children had crossed the path.","孩子们穿过小路前，训犬员用牵引绳控制住兴奋的狗。","Restrain means prevent a person or animal from moving freely.","With states the means; until marks the end of the control.","The dog is physically held back for safety.") ,C("restrain.s2","情緒","Although angry, Mara restrained herself from sending the message until she had checked the facts.","尽管生气，Mara 还是克制住自己，没有立刻发消息，而是先核实事实。","Restrain oneself from an action means control an impulse.","Although contrasts feeling with action; from introduces the avoided act.","This is self-control, not physical restraint.") ,C("restrain.s1","法律","The court issued an order to restrain the company from dumping waste into the river.","法院发布禁令，禁止该公司向河中倾倒废物。","Restrain can mean legally prevent an action.","From dumping names the prohibited conduct.","This is the legal prevention sense.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","Mara restrained herself to sending the angry message before checking the facts.","Mara restrained herself from sending the angry message before checking the facts.","Restrain oneself from doing something is the standard construction.")],quiz:[Q("restrain.q1","restrain.s1","meaning","A handler restrains a dog by ___.",["holding it back from moving freely","teaching it to swim","recording its bark"],"holding it back from moving freely","This is the physical-control sense.","meaning"),Q("restrain.q2","restrain.s2","context","He restrained himself from interrupting, so he ___.",["controlled the urge to speak","shouted over the speaker","left the room to buy food"],"controlled the urge to speak","This is the self-control sense.","context"),Q("restrain.q3","restrain.s1","collocation","The order restrained the factory ____ releasing untreated water.",["from","at","to"],"from","Restrain someone from doing an action is standard.","collocation"),Q("restrain.q4","restrain.s2","meaning","Which example shows emotional restraint?",["She held back an angry reply.","A guard locked the gate.","A strap stopped the suitcase moving."],"She held back an angry reply.","The person controls an impulse rather than a body or object.","meaning")]});
D("restraint",{etymology:E("From Old French restreinte and Latin restringere ‘bind tight’; English uses restraint for physical control and for self-control or moderation.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restraint"),contexts:[C("restraint.s1","安全","The nurse used a soft wrist restraint only while the confused patient was at immediate risk of pulling out the line.","只有在意识混乱的患者有立即拔掉输液管的危险时，护士才使用柔软的腕部约束带。","A restraint is a device or measure that limits movement.","Only while limits the use to a specific risk; of pulling out gives the danger.","This is the physical-device sense.") ,C("restraint.s2","溝通","The director criticized the proposal with restraint, noting its weaknesses without insulting its authors.","主任克制地批评了提案，只指出缺点而没有侮辱作者。","Restraint can mean self-control or moderation.","With restraint modifies criticized and describes the manner.","The speaker controls the tone.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The driver showed restraint by accelerating through the crowded school crossing without slowing down.","The driver showed poor restraint by accelerating through the crowded school crossing without slowing down.","Restraint means control or moderation; reckless acceleration is evidence of its absence.")],quiz:[Q("restraint.q1","restraint.s1","meaning","A safety restraint is used to ___.",["limit movement to prevent immediate harm","measure the room's temperature","identify a survey participant"],"limit movement to prevent immediate harm","This is the device or control sense.","meaning"),Q("restraint.q2","restraint.s2","context","A critic who speaks with restraint ___.",["expresses criticism in a controlled way","shouts personal insults","refuses to consider evidence"],"expresses criticism in a controlled way","This is the self-control sense.","context"),Q("restraint.q3","restraint.s1","meaning","Which is an example of a physical restraint?",["A seat belt holding a passenger securely","A polite pause before replying","A budget limit on advertising"],"A seat belt holding a passenger securely","A seat belt physically limits movement for safety.","meaning"),Q("restraint.q4","restraint.s2","collocation","The spokesperson answered the accusation with admirable ____.",["restraint","restroom","retention"],"restraint","With restraint describes a controlled response.","collocation")]});
D("restrict",{etymology:E("From Latin restringere ‘bind back, confine’, re- ‘back’ + stringere ‘bind tight’; it means limit the range, amount, or freedom of something.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restrict"),contexts:[C("restrict.s1","政策","The city restricted heavy trucks from entering the old bridge during the repair work.","维修期间，市政府限制重型卡车驶入这座旧桥。","Restrict means place a limit on an action or access.","From entering introduces the prohibited action; during sets the period.","The city limits vehicle access.") ,C("restrict.s2","飲食","Her doctor advised her to restrict salt because it worsened her blood pressure.","医生建议她限制盐的摄入，因为盐会使血压恶化。","Restrict can mean limit the amount of something used or consumed.","To restrict takes salt as object; because explains the medical reason.","The amount consumed is reduced.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The notice restricts visitors enter the laboratory after 6 p.m.","The notice restricts visitors from entering the laboratory after 6 p.m.","Restrict a person from doing something takes from before the gerund.")],quiz:[Q("restrict.q1","restrict.s1","meaning","A sign restricts access to a laboratory when it ___.",["limits who may enter","lists the lab's opening music","measures the floor's length"],"limits who may enter","Restrict means impose a limit.","meaning"),Q("restrict.q2","restrict.s2","context","A doctor tells a patient to restrict caffeine. The patient should ___.",["limit how much caffeine they consume","drink more at every meal","measure the doctor's height"],"limit how much caffeine they consume","The second sense is limiting an amount.","context"),Q("restrict.q3","restrict.s1","collocation","The rule restricts drivers ____ parking near the gate.",["from","at","with"],"from","Restrict someone from doing something is the standard pattern.","collocation"),Q("restrict.q4","restrict.s2","meaning","Which sentence uses restrict to mean limit an amount?",["The recipe restricts sugar to one spoonful.","The fence restricts access to the garden.","The guard restricts visitors from entering."],"The recipe restricts sugar to one spoonful.","The quantity of sugar is capped.","meaning") ]});
D("restricted",{etymology:E("Past participle and adjective from restrict, from Latin restringere ‘bind back, confine’; it describes something limited by a rule or boundary.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restricted"),contexts:[C("restricted.s1","公共場所","The archive keeps restricted documents in a locked room that only registered researchers may enter.","档案馆把限制查阅的文件存放在上锁房间，只有登记研究人员可以进入。","Restricted means limited in access or use.","That-clause identifies who may enter; only emphasizes the limit.","The documents are not generally available.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The restricted files is available only to senior staff.","The restricted files are available only to senior staff.","Files is plural and requires are.")],quiz:[Q("restricted.q1","restricted.s1","meaning","A restricted area is one that ___.",["only authorized people may enter","is open to every passerby","has no boundaries or rules"],"only authorized people may enter","Restricted means limited by access rules.","meaning"),Q("restricted.q2","restricted.s1","context","A restricted document may be read by ___.",["people who have permission","anyone who happens to pass it","no one under any circumstances"],"people who have permission","The access is limited, not necessarily impossible.","context"),Q("restricted.q3","restricted.s1","grammar","Choose the correct sentence.",["The restricted files are locked.","The restricted files is locked.","The restricted files was locked yesterday."],"The restricted files are locked.","Plural files takes are.","grammar"),Q("restricted.q4","restricted.s1","meaning","A restricted diet is one with ___.",["limits on certain foods","no meals at all by definition","only restaurant reviews"],"limits on certain foods","The adjective describes an imposed limit.","meaning")]});
