D("restroom",{etymology:E("A 20th-century American euphemistic compound of rest + room, naming a public room with toilet facilities.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/restroom"),contexts:[C("restroom.s1","公共場所","The museum's ground-floor restroom has a changing table beside the accessible washbasin.","博物馆一楼的洗手间在无障碍洗手池旁设有婴儿护理台。","A restroom is a public room with a toilet and washbasin.","Ground-floor locates it; has introduces its facilities.","This is the North American public-facility sense.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","Visitors washed their hands at the restroom, then went back to view the paintings.","Visitors washed their hands in the restroom, then went back to view the paintings.","People are in a restroom; at would usually identify the building or place more broadly.")],quiz:[Q("restroom.q1","restroom.s1","meaning","A museum restroom is a room where visitors can ___.",["use a toilet and washbasin","borrow a sculpture","buy a train ticket"],"use a toilet and washbasin","Restroom is a polite term for a public toilet room.","meaning"),Q("restroom.q2","restroom.s1","context","A traveler asks where the restroom is because they need to ___.",["wash their hands or use the toilet","check into a resort","answer a survey"],"wash their hands or use the toilet","This is the public-facility sense.","context"),Q("restroom.q3","restroom.s1","collocation","The child went ____ the restroom to wash up.",["into","across","between"],"into","Into indicates movement inside the room.","collocation"),Q("restroom.q4","restroom.s1","meaning","In a North American station, a sign marked Restroom points to ___.",["a public toilet room","a room for sleeping passengers","a staff office for survey respondents"],"a public toilet room","Restroom is a common euphemistic label for public toilet facilities.","meaning")]});
D("result",{etymology:E("From Latin resultare ‘spring back, rebound’, from re- ‘back’ + saltare ‘leap’; English developed the senses outcome, score, and happen as a consequence.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/result"),contexts:[C("result.s1","調查","The result of the soil test showed that the garden needed less fertilizer than expected.","土壤检测结果表明，花园所需肥料比预期少。","A result is something caused or established by an action or test.","Of the soil test identifies what produced the finding; that-clause reports it.","This is an outcome or finding.") ,C("result.s2","考試","Mika checked her exam result online before calling her family.","Mika 在给家人打电话前先在线查看了考试成绩。","A result can be a score or mark in an exam or game.","Exam modifies result and specifies the measurement context.","This is a score, not a general outcome.") ,C("result.s3","科學","Small cracks resulted from repeated freezing and thawing of the pipe.","管道反复冻融导致了细小裂缝。","As a verb, result means happen or exist because of something else.","From introduces the cause; the verb is intransitive.","The cracks arose as a consequence of freeze-thaw cycles.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The hairline cracks resulted of repeated freezing and thawing.","The hairline cracks resulted from repeated freezing and thawing.","The verb result uses from before its cause.")],quiz:[Q("result.q1","result.s1","meaning","The result of a soil test is ___.",["the finding it produces","the machine used to dig soil","a person who takes a survey"],"the finding it produces","A result is an outcome or finding.","meaning"),Q("result.q2","result.s2","context","A student asks when exam results will be posted. They want to know ___.",["their scores or marks","the names of the exam writers only","how to enter a restroom"],"their scores or marks","This is the score/mark sense.","context"),Q("result.q3","result.s3","collocation","The delay resulted ____ a broken signal cable.",["from","at","into"],"from","Result from introduces the cause of an event.","collocation"),Q("result.q4","result.s1","meaning","Which use of result names an outcome rather than a score?",["The result of the survey surprised the council.","Her exam result was 92 percent.","The match result was two goals to one."],"The result of the survey surprised the council.","A survey finding is a general outcome.","meaning") ]});
D("result in",{etymology:E("Phrasal verb formed from result, from Latin resultare ‘rebound’, + in; it means cause a particular outcome.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/result"),contexts:[C("result in.s1","工程","A loose cable can result in a sudden loss of power when the machine starts.","机器启动时，松动的电缆可能导致突然断电。","Result in means cause something to happen.","In introduces the outcome; when gives the triggering condition.","The cable is the cause and power loss is its consequence.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","A loose cable can result to a sudden loss of power.","A loose cable can result in a sudden loss of power.","Result in introduces the consequence; result from introduces the cause.")],quiz:[Q("result in.q1","result in.s1","meaning","Poor drainage may result in ___.",["flooded paths","better drainage by itself","a survey answer"],"flooded paths","Result in means cause an outcome.","meaning"),Q("result in.q2","result in.s1","context","What can result in a road closure?",["A fallen tree blocking both lanes","A sign saying the road is open","A driver's unrelated birthday"],"A fallen tree blocking both lanes","The tree can cause the closure.","context"),Q("result in.q3","result in.s1","collocation","The error resulted ____ an incorrect total.",["in","from","at"],"in","Result in is followed by the consequence.","collocation"),Q("result in.q4","result in.s1","meaning","Choose the sentence where result in means 'cause'.",["The leak resulted in water damage.","The water damage resulted from a leak.","The result of the test was printed."],"The leak resulted in water damage.","The phrase introduces the consequence, water damage.","meaning")]});
D("resultant",{etymology:E("From Latin resultantem, present participle of resultare ‘rebound’; English uses it as an adjective for something produced as a direct consequence.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resultant"),contexts:[C("resultant.s1","科學","The resultant heat melted the thin wax layer after the two chemicals were mixed.","两种化学物质混合后，产生的热量融化了薄薄的蜡层。","Resultant means occurring as the direct result of something.","After marks the sequence; resultant modifies heat produced by mixing.","The heat is the consequence of the reaction.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The resultant leak caused the pipe to crack later, so the leak was the original event rather than its consequence.","The initial crack caused a resultant leak, so the leak was the consequence rather than the original event.","Resultant describes an effect that follows from a cause.")],quiz:[Q("resultant.q1","resultant.s1","meaning","Resultant damage is damage that ___.",["happens as a consequence","causes every earlier event","has no connection to an event"],"happens as a consequence","Resultant means produced by something else.","meaning"),Q("resultant.q2","resultant.s1","context","A storm knocks down a tree, which damages a fence. The fence damage is ___.",["resultant damage from the storm","the cause of the storm","a survey response"],"resultant damage from the storm","The fence damage is the consequence.","context"),Q("resultant.q3","resultant.s1","word-formation","The word resultant is related to the verb ___.",["result","respond","retire"],"result","Resultant derives from result.","word-formation"),Q("resultant.q4","resultant.s1","meaning","Choose the phrase meaning 'the direct effect'.",["the resultant pressure change","the unrelated initial measurement","the planned cause of the experiment"],"the resultant pressure change","Resultant identifies an effect produced by a cause.","meaning")]});
D("resume",{etymology:E("From French résumer and Latin resumere, re- ‘again’ + sumere ‘take’; the verb means take up again, return to a position, or give a brief summary.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resume"),contexts:[C("resume.s1","會議","After the fire alarm was cleared, the chair resumed the meeting at the point where discussion had stopped.","火警解除后，主席从讨论中断处继续开会。","Resume means start again after a pause.","After gives the interruption; at the point specifies where activity began again.","The meeting continues rather than beginning from the start.") ,C("resume.s2","工作","At noon, the judge resumed her seat and invited the next witness to speak.","中午，法官回到座位上，并请下一位证人发言。","Resume can mean go back to a seat or post.","Her seat is the direct object; and links the next action.","The judge returns to the position she had left.") ,C("resume.s3","演講","Before questions began, the lecturer gave a brief resume of the argument's main stages.","提问开始前，讲师简要概述了论证的主要阶段。","Resume can also be a short summary of a speech, book, or argument.","Of the argument identifies the material summarized.","Here it is a noun meaning summary.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The lecture resumed of its three main claims before questions began.","The lecturer gave a resume of the three main claims before questions began.","Resume meaning summary is a noun; a lecture can resume, but it does not resume of its claims.")],quiz:[Q("resume.q1","resume.s1","meaning","After an interruption, to resume a meeting is to ___.",["start it again","write a list of job qualifications","end it permanently"],"start it again","The verb's main sense is take up again.","meaning"),Q("resume.q2","resume.s2","context","The judge resumed her seat means she ___.",["returned to the seat","left the courtroom for good","summarized the case"],"returned to the seat","Resume can mean go back to a position.","context"),Q("resume.q3","resume.s3","meaning","A short resume of a lecture is ___.",["a summary of its main points","a second microphone","a person who answered a survey"],"a summary of its main points","This is the noun summary sense.","meaning"),Q("resume.q4","resume.s1","collocation","The orchestra paused for the announcement, then ____ the symphony.",["resumed","resulted","restroom"],"resumed","Resume an activity means continue it after a pause.","collocation")]});
D("résumé",{etymology:E("From French résumé, past participle of résumer ‘summarize’, from Latin resumere ‘take up again’; the noun is a concise summary or record of qualifications.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resume"),contexts:[C("résumé.s1","求職","Leila tailored her résumé to the engineering post, placing her laboratory experience above unrelated summer jobs.","Leila 根据工程职位调整简历，把实验室经历放在无关的暑期工作之前。","A résumé is a brief document listing education, jobs, and skills.","To the post states the document's purpose; placing explains its organization.","The document presents qualifications to an employer.") ,C("résumé.s2","寫作","The chair began with a résumé of the debate before announcing the vote.","主席在宣布表决前先简要概述了辩论内容。","Résumé can mean a short summary of what was said or written.","Of the debate identifies the material summarized; before marks the order.","This is the summary sense, not a job document.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The applicant attached a résumé of the debate listing her degrees and previous employers.","The applicant attached a résumé listing her degrees and previous employers.","A job résumé records a person's qualifications; a résumé of a debate is a summary of that discussion.")],quiz:[Q("résumé.q1","résumé.s1","meaning","A job applicant's résumé normally contains ___.",["education, experience, and skills","the full text of a court trial","a list of restaurant menus"],"education, experience, and skills","The document presents professional qualifications.","meaning"),Q("résumé.q2","résumé.s2","context","A résumé of a meeting is ___.",["a brief summary of what happened","a person's job history","a medical treatment"],"a brief summary of what happened","The second sense is a concise account of prior discussion.","context"),Q("résumé.q3","résumé.s1","collocation","She sent her résumé ____ the hiring manager.",["to","at","from"],"to","Send a résumé to someone is the standard construction.","collocation"),Q("résumé.q4","résumé.s1","meaning","Which detail belongs on a job résumé?",["A certificate relevant to the vacancy","A summary of a recent debate","A list of the applicant's favorite restaurants"],"A certificate relevant to the vacancy","A résumé lists qualifications pertinent to employment.","meaning")]});
D("resumption",{etymology:E("From resume + -tion, via Latin resumptio, from resumere ‘take up again’; the noun denotes the restarting of an interrupted activity.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resumption"),contexts:[C("resumption.s1","交通","The resumption of ferry service depended on the harbor master confirming that the storm had passed.","渡轮能否恢复运营，取决于港务长是否确认风暴已经过去。","Resumption is the restart of an activity that had stopped.","Of ferry service identifies what restarts; depended on gives the condition.","Service had been interrupted and may begin again.")],mistakes:[M("word form","The resumption of ferry service were delayed by high winds.","The resumption of ferry service was delayed by high winds.","Resumption is a singular noun and takes was.")],quiz:[Q("resumption.q1","resumption.s1","meaning","The resumption of talks means ___.",["the talks start again after a pause","the talks are translated","the speakers retire permanently"],"the talks start again after a pause","Resumption is a restart after an interruption.","meaning"),Q("resumption.q2","resumption.s1","context","A notice says resumption of trains is at 6 a.m. What happens then?",["Train service starts again","The last train is canceled","Passengers take a survey"],"Train service starts again","The service resumes after being stopped.","context"),Q("resumption.q3","resumption.s1","word-formation","Resumption is a noun related to the verb ___.",["resume","respect","retract"],"resume","Resumption names the act of resuming.","word-formation"),Q("resumption.q4","resumption.s1","grammar","Choose the correct agreement.",["The resumption was announced.","The resumption were announced.","The resumption are announced yesterday."],"The resumption was announced.","The singular noun resumption takes was.","grammar")]});
D("resurrection",{etymology:E("From Latin resurrectio, from resurrectus, past participle of resurgere ‘rise again’, re- ‘again’ + surgere ‘rise’; English uses it literally and figuratively.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resurrection"),contexts:[C("resurrection.s1","文化","The museum's exhibition traced the resurrection of hand weaving, which returned to local workshops after decades of decline.","博物馆展览追溯了手工织布业的复兴；它在衰退数十年后重回当地作坊。","Resurrection can mean revival of a practice, career, or idea.","Which clause identifies the revived practice; after gives its earlier decline.","The craft becomes active again after having nearly disappeared.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The magazine called the canceled festival a resurrection even though it never returned or took place again.","The magazine called the canceled festival's return the following year a resurrection.","A figurative resurrection is a revival; an event that never returns has not been revived.")],quiz:[Q("resurrection.q1","resurrection.s1","meaning","The resurrection of a forgotten craft is ___.",["its revival after decline","its first invention","its permanent disappearance"],"its revival after decline","The figurative sense is a return to activity.","meaning"),Q("resurrection.q2","resurrection.s1","context","A newspaper calls a revived neighborhood theater a resurrection because it ___.",["opened again after years of closure","was built for the first time yesterday","has never existed"],"opened again after years of closure","The theater has returned after a period of absence.","context"),Q("resurrection.q3","resurrection.s1","word-formation","The Latin element re- in resurrection contributes ___.",["again","under","without"],"again","The historical formation carries the idea of rising again.","word-formation"),Q("resurrection.q4","resurrection.s1","meaning","Which use is figurative rather than literal?",["the resurrection of a once-popular dance style","a religious claim about rising from the dead","a medical report about a person who stopped breathing"],"the resurrection of a once-popular dance style","A dance style can be revived metaphorically.","meaning")]});
D("resuscitate",{etymology:E("From Latin resuscitare, re- ‘again’ + suscitare ‘rouse, raise’; the verb means restore a person to life or revive an inactive system or idea.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/resuscitate"),contexts:[C("resuscitate.s1","急救","The lifeguard began CPR to resuscitate the swimmer who had stopped breathing.","游泳者停止呼吸后，救生员开始心肺复苏，试图使其恢复生命体征。","Resuscitate means restore a person who has stopped breathing or appears lifeless.","To resuscitate gives the purpose of CPR; who-clause identifies the swimmer's condition.","This is the emergency medical sense.") ,C("resuscitate.s2","經濟","A small grant resuscitated the village's closed cinema, allowing weekend screenings to return.","一笔小额拨款使村里关闭的电影院重新活跃起来，周末放映得以恢复。","Resuscitate can mean make an activity, system, or idea active again.","Allowing states the practical result of the grant.","The cinema is figuratively revived.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The funding resuscitated the cinema by permanently closing it and ending all screenings.","The funding resuscitated the cinema by reopening it and restoring weekend screenings.","To resuscitate an institution is to revive it, not close it permanently.")],quiz:[Q("resuscitate.q1","resuscitate.s1","meaning","To resuscitate a person in an emergency is to ___.",["try to restore breathing or circulation","write a summary of their job history","restrict access to a building"],"try to restore breathing or circulation","This is the life-saving medical sense.","meaning"),Q("resuscitate.q2","resuscitate.s2","context","A grant resuscitates a closed library when it ___.",["helps the library reopen and serve readers again","removes its books permanently","changes its name but keeps it closed"],"helps the library reopen and serve readers again","The figurative sense means revive an inactive service.","context"),Q("resuscitate.q3","resuscitate.s1","word-formation","The prefix re- in resuscitate conveys ___.",["again","against","before"],"again","The verb carries the idea of rousing again.","word-formation"),Q("resuscitate.q4","resuscitate.s2","meaning","Which uses resuscitate figuratively?",["The campaign resuscitated interest in local history.","The medic tried to resuscitate the swimmer.","The doctor checked the patient's respiration."],"The campaign resuscitated interest in local history.","Interest can be revived metaphorically.","meaning")]});
D("retail",{etymology:E("From Old French retaillier, re- ‘back’ + taillier ‘cut’; the verb once meant cut off a piece, and the business term developed for selling goods in small amounts to the public.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retail"),contexts:[C("retail.s1","商業","The farm sells its cheese wholesale to shops but keeps one stall to retail small batches directly to visitors.","农场把奶酪批发给商店，但保留一个摊位直接向游客零售小批量产品。","Retail is the business of selling goods to the public in small quantities.","But contrasts wholesale with retail; directly to visitors identifies the customers.","This sentence uses retail as a verb.") ,C("retail.s2","定價","The retailer's suggested retail price includes tax but excludes home delivery.","零售商建议零售价含税，但不含送货上门费用。","Retail can modify a price connected with selling to the public.","Suggested retail price is a noun phrase; retail modifies price.","This is the adjective/price sense.") ,C("retail.s3","商業","These handmade lamps retail for about eighty dollars in city shops.","这些手工灯在城里的商店零售价约为80美元。","As a verb, retail can say what price an item sells for.","For introduces the sale price.","This is the intransitive price sense.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","A wholesaler sells single jars directly to household shoppers as retail, in very large batches to other distributors.","A wholesaler sells very large batches to other distributors; a retailer sells goods to household shoppers in smaller quantities.","Retail refers to sales to the public in small amounts; bulk distributor sales are wholesale.")],quiz:[Q("retail.q1","retail.s1","meaning","Retail sales are usually made ___.",["to the public in small quantities","only between manufacturers in bulk","by survey respondents to courts"],"to the public in small quantities","This is the core retail-business sense.","meaning"),Q("retail.q2","retail.s2","context","A retail price is the price ___.",["charged to the public by a shop","paid by a factory for raw metal","used to score a match"],"charged to the public by a shop","Retail modifies price for a consumer sale.","context"),Q("retail.q3","retail.s3","grammar","The jackets retail ____ $60 each.",["for","to","at by"],"for","Retail for a price is the usual intransitive construction.","grammar"),Q("retail.q4","retail.s1","meaning","Which transaction is retail?",["A bookshop sells one book to a reader.","A mill sells ten thousand sheets to a distributor.","A mine sells ore to a steelworks in bulk."],"A bookshop sells one book to a reader.","Retail is sale to the end public in small quantities.","meaning")]});
D("retailer",{etymology:E("From retail + agent suffix -er, formed from the verb retail, which came through Old French retaillier ‘cut in pieces’.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retailer"),contexts:[C("retailer.s1","商業","The online retailer let customers return the lamp to a nearby shop instead of mailing it back.","这家网上零售商允许顾客把灯退到附近门店，而不必邮寄回去。","A retailer is a person or company that sells goods directly to the public.","Let takes customers as object; instead of contrasts the two return methods.","The company sells to final consumers.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The steel mill was a retailer because it sold huge shipments of raw steel only to manufacturers.","The steel mill was a wholesaler because it sold huge shipments of raw steel only to manufacturers.","A retailer sells to the public; bulk business-to-business sales are wholesale.")],quiz:[Q("retailer.q1","retailer.s1","meaning","A retailer sells goods ___.",["directly to members of the public","only to another factory in huge lots","only to courts"],"directly to members of the public","The source sense defines a retailer as a seller to the public.","meaning"),Q("retailer.q2","retailer.s1","context","Which business is a retailer?",["A shop selling shoes to walk-in customers","A mine selling ore to a smelter in bulk","A farm selling grain to a national distributor"],"A shop selling shoes to walk-in customers","The shoe shop sells directly to consumers.","context"),Q("retailer.q3","retailer.s1","word-formation","The suffix -er in retailer names ___.",["a person or business that performs an activity","the quality of being retail","a past event"],"a person or business that performs an activity","-er forms an agent noun from retail.","word-formation"),Q("retailer.q4","retailer.s1","meaning","A retailer differs from a wholesaler because a retailer typically sells ___.",["to the end customer","only raw materials to factories","services to court respondents"],"to the end customer","Retailers serve the public rather than bulk distributors.","meaning")]});
D("retain",{etymology:E("From Old French retenir and Latin retinere, re- ‘back’ + tenere ‘hold’; it means keep, preserve, remember, or keep a professional engaged.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retain"),contexts:[C("retain.s1","建築","The renovated station retained its original stone clock even after the platforms were rebuilt.","车站翻新后保留了原有的石制时钟，尽管站台已经重建。","Retain means continue to have something and not lose it.","Even after contrasts the preserved clock with the rebuilt platforms.","The clock remains part of the station.") ,C("retain.s2","教育","Students retain new vocabulary better when they use it in a sentence the same day.","学生在当天把新词用进句子里，记得会更牢。","Retain can mean keep learned facts in memory.","Better compares memory outcomes; when introduces the practice that helps.","The sense concerns remembering information.") ,C("retain.s3","法律","The startup retained a patent lawyer before negotiating the licensing agreement.","这家初创公司在谈许可协议前聘请了一位专利律师。","To retain a professional is to pay or formally engage them to work for you.","Before places the engagement ahead of negotiations.","This is the professional-services sense.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The startup retained to a lawyer to review its patent agreement.","The startup retained a lawyer to review its patent agreement.","Retain meaning hire takes the professional as a direct object, without to.")],quiz:[Q("retain.q1","retain.s1","meaning","A building retains a historic doorway if it ___.",["keeps it rather than removing it","replaces it with a parking lot","forgets where it was"],"keeps it rather than removing it","Retain means continue to have or preserve.","meaning"),Q("retain.q2","retain.s2","context","A student retains a formula when they ___.",["can remember it later","erase every note about it","hire a lawyer to explain it"],"can remember it later","This is the memory sense.","context"),Q("retain.q3","retain.s3","grammar","The firm retained ____ to review the contract.",["a lawyer","to a lawyer","lawyer to"],"a lawyer","Retain meaning hire takes a direct object.","grammar"),Q("retain.q4","retain.s1","meaning","Which sentence uses retain to mean keep possession?",["The museum retained the original receipt.","The pupil retained the poem in memory.","The company retained counsel."],"The museum retained the original receipt.","The receipt remains in the museum's possession.","meaning")]});
D("retake",{etymology:E("Formed from re- ‘again’ + take; the verb means take an exam again or take back a place or object that was lost.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retake"),contexts:[C("retake.s1","教育","After reviewing the missed questions, Omar retook the chemistry exam the following Friday.","复习了做错的题目后，Omar 在下周五重考了化学。","Retake means take an examination again.","After gives the preparation; the following Friday marks the later attempt.","This is an additional attempt at the same test.") ,C("retake.s2","歷史","The troops retook the bridge after engineers cleared the explosives from its supports.","工程师清除桥墩上的炸药后，部队重新夺回了这座桥。","Retake can mean take back a place or thing that was lost.","After marks the condition that allowed the recovery.","The bridge had been lost and was captured again.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","After scoring poorly, Omar retook a completely different exam he had never attempted before.","After scoring poorly, Omar retook the chemistry exam he had already taken once.","Retake means take the same examination again, not take a different exam for the first time.")],quiz:[Q("retake.q1","retake.s1","meaning","A student retakes a test when they ___.",["take that examination again","write a résumé for a teacher","leave the classroom forever"],"take that examination again","This is the repeat-exam sense.","meaning"),Q("retake.q2","retake.s2","context","The army retook a fort after losing it. The army ___.",["captured the fort again","built a different fort from scratch","retired from the area permanently"],"captured the fort again","Retake can mean capture a lost place again.","context"),Q("retake.q3","retake.s1","word-formation","The prefix re- in retake indicates ___.",["doing the taking again","taking something apart","taking something away"],"doing the taking again","Here re- means again.","word-formation"),Q("retake.q4","retake.s2","meaning","Which event is a retaking of territory?",["A city is recaptured after an enemy occupation.","A student sits a new language exam.","A shop takes payment for a return."],"A city is recaptured after an enemy occupation.","The place is taken back after being lost.","meaning")]});
D("retaliate",{etymology:E("From Latin retaliatus, past participle of retaliare ‘pay back in kind’, from talio ‘like-for-like retaliation’; it means answer harm or an insult with a similar act.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retaliate"),contexts:[C("retaliate.s1","外交","The government promised not to retaliate against neighboring fishermen for an accidental border crossing.","政府承诺不会因邻国渔民意外越界而进行报复。","Retaliate means harm or attack in return for harm done.","Against names the target; for gives the triggering act.","The response would be a counter-harm.") ,C("retaliate.s2","溝通","Instead of retaliating with another insult, Priya asked her colleague to explain the remark.","Priya 没有再用侮辱的话回击，而是请同事解释那句话。","Retaliate can mean answer an unkind act with a similar act.","Instead of contrasts the avoided response; with introduces its possible form.","This is verbal retaliation.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The village retaliated the raid by sending a formal complaint to the council.","The village retaliated for the raid by taking a similar harmful action against the attackers.","Retaliate for names the harm answered; retaliate against names the target, and a mere complaint is not itself a counterattack.")],quiz:[Q("retaliate.q1","retaliate.s1","meaning","To retaliate after an attack is to ___.",["harm or attack in return","offer an unrelated apology","write a résumé"],"harm or attack in return","This is the counter-harm sense.","meaning"),Q("retaliate.q2","retaliate.s2","context","A colleague answers a cruel joke with a similarly cutting remark. The colleague ___.",["retaliates verbally","retains the joke in memory","resumes the meeting"],"retaliates verbally","This is the sense of answering an unkind act with a similar one.","context"),Q("retaliate.q3","retaliate.s1","collocation","The group threatened to retaliate ____ the attackers.",["against","at to","for with"],"against","Retaliate against identifies the target.","collocation"),Q("retaliate.q4","retaliate.s2","meaning","Which is retaliation rather than a neutral reply?",["Answering a deliberate insult with another insult","Thanking someone for useful feedback","Asking what a word means"],"Answering a deliberate insult with another insult","The response mirrors the unkind act.","meaning")]});
D("retaliation",{etymology:E("From retaliate + -ion, via French rétaliation and Latin retaliare ‘pay back in kind’; the noun names an act of harmful reprisal.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retaliation"),contexts:[C("retaliation.s1","職場","The employee reported that his schedule was cut in retaliation for raising a safety concern.","员工报告说，他的班次被削减，是因为提出安全问题而遭到报复。","Retaliation is harmful action taken in response to an earlier complaint or injury.","In retaliation for links the harm to its stated trigger.","The schedule cut is a reprisal for speaking up.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The manager called a fair promotion retaliation even though it rewarded the employee for strong work and punished nobody.","The manager called the schedule cut retaliation because it punished the employee for raising a safety concern.","Retaliation is harmful reprisal for an earlier act, not a fair reward.")],quiz:[Q("retaliation.q1","retaliation.s1","meaning","An act of retaliation is ___.",["a harmful reprisal for something done earlier","a neutral reply to a question","a summary of a meeting"],"a harmful reprisal for something done earlier","The noun describes payback in response to prior harm or action.","meaning"),Q("retaliation.q2","retaliation.s1","context","A worker is punished for filing a safety complaint. This may be ___.",["retaliation","restoration","resumption"],"retaliation","The punishment is reprisal for the complaint.","context"),Q("retaliation.q3","retaliation.s1","collocation","The policy prohibits ____ against employees who report hazards.",["retaliation","retail","retreat"],"retaliation","Retaliation against someone is the standard phrase.","collocation"),Q("retaliation.q4","retaliation.s1","meaning","Which event is most clearly retaliation?",["A landlord raises rent because a tenant reported a code violation.","A landlord fixes a leak after receiving a request.","A tenant answers a survey about housing."],"A landlord raises rent because a tenant reported a code violation.","The harmful action is taken in response to the report.","meaning")]});
D("retard",{etymology:E("From Latin retardare ‘delay’, re- ‘back’ + tardare ‘make slow’; as a verb it means slow progress, while its historical noun use for a person is now an offensive slur.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retard"),contexts:[C("retard.s1","生物","Cold temperatures can retard the growth of seedlings without killing them.","低温会减缓幼苗生长，但不一定会使幼苗死亡。","Retard means slow the progress or development of something.","Without contrasts delay with destruction.","This is the transitive verb sense.") ,C("retard.s2","歷史","The report said that work retarded during the winter because roads were impassable.","报告称，冬季道路无法通行，工程进展因此放缓。","As an intransitive verb, retard means move or happen more slowly.","During the winter marks when progress slowed; because gives the cause.","Here the process itself slowed.") ,C("retard.s3","語域","A language guide warns that the noun retard is a slur and must not be used to label a person.","语言指南警告说，名词 retard 是侮辱性称呼，不应拿来指人。","The noun sense is an offensive historical label for a person with learning difficulties.","That-clause reports the guide's warning; the quoted word is discussed, not directed at anyone.","This use is derogatory and should be avoided.")],mistakes:[M("register","The editor told a colleague, 'You are a retard,' as a harmless technical description.","The editor used respectful, specific language and did not apply the slur to a colleague.","The noun is an offensive slur, not a neutral technical description.")],quiz:[Q("retard.q1","retard.s1","meaning","A chemical may retard rusting when it ___.",["slows its progress","makes it happen instantly","turns rust into a résumé"],"slows its progress","The verb means slow the progress of something.","meaning"),Q("retard.q2","retard.s2","context","If economic growth retards during a crisis, it ___.",["moves or happens more slowly","accelerates sharply","is sold in a retail shop"],"moves or happens more slowly","This is the intransitive sense of slowing down.","context"),Q("retard.q3","retard.s3","register","How should the historical noun use of retard for a person be treated?",["As an offensive slur to avoid","As a polite clinical term today","As a neutral job title"],"As an offensive slur to avoid","The source marks this use as offensive and outdated.","register"),Q("retard.q4","retard.s1","collocation","A lack of sunlight can ____ the growth of a plant.",["retard","resound","resume"],"retard","Retard growth means slow its development.","collocation")]});
D("retardation",{etymology:E("From retard + -ation; retard comes from Latin retardare ‘delay’, and the noun describes slowing or delayed growth or learning.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retardation"),contexts:[C("retardation.s1","植物學","The botanist linked retardation of root growth to waterlogged soil rather than to a lack of seed.","植物学家把根系生长迟缓归因于土壤积水，而不是缺少种子。","Retardation is the process of slowing progress or a delay in growth.","Of root growth specifies what slowed; rather than contrasts the rejected cause.","This is a technical description of delayed plant development.")],mistakes:[M("register","The report described a person as having mental retardation, using the phrase as its preferred modern label.","The report used current respectful wording, such as intellectual disability, rather than an outdated label.","Although historically used in clinical language, this label is now outdated and can be offensive when applied to people.")],quiz:[Q("retardation.q1","retardation.s1","meaning","Retardation of seedling growth means ___.",["growth is delayed or slowed","the seedlings have been transplanted","the soil has been sold"],"growth is delayed or slowed","The noun denotes slowed progress or development.","meaning"),Q("retardation.q2","retardation.s1","context","A study reports retardation of learning after sleep loss. It found learning ___.",["proceeded more slowly","became a restaurant","was resumed from the beginning"],"proceeded more slowly","The term describes a delay in learning progress.","context"),Q("retardation.q3","retardation.s1","word-formation","Retardation is formed from retard plus a suffix that creates ___.",["a process or state noun","a plural agent noun","a past-tense verb"],"a process or state noun","-ation forms a noun naming an action or process.","word-formation"),Q("retardation.q4","retardation.s1","register","When discussing a person's disability today, which expression is preferred?",["intellectual disability","a historical slur","a delay in plant roots"],"intellectual disability","The people-related historical label is outdated; use current respectful language.","register")]});
D("retarded",{etymology:E("Past participle and adjective from retard, from Latin retardare ‘delay’; it can describe delayed development, but its former clinical label for a person is outdated and insulting.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retarded"),contexts:[C("retarded.s1","生物","The paper recorded retarded growth in the seedlings exposed to salt, comparing them with untreated plants.","论文记录了受盐处理的幼苗生长迟缓，并将其与未处理植株作比较。","Retarded can describe development happening more slowly than expected.","Exposed to identifies the condition; comparing states the control.","The adjective modifies plant growth, not a person.") ,C("retarded.s2","語域","A historical chart used the word retarded for a patient; current clinicians avoid that label because it is insulting.","一份旧病历曾用 retarded 描述患者；如今临床人员避免这个称呼，因为它具有侮辱性。","This is an outdated clinical label for intellectual disability and is insulting when applied to a person.","The semicolon contrasts historical wording with current practice.","The word is mentioned critically, never as a respectful label.")],mistakes:[M("register","The teacher described a pupil as retarded in a current report, treating the term as a neutral diagnosis.","The teacher used current respectful language, such as a student with an intellectual disability, in the report.","The person-label is outdated and insulting; describe the person respectfully and specifically.")],quiz:[Q("retarded.q1","retarded.s1","meaning","Retarded growth in a plant means the plant's development is ___.",["slower than expected","faster than all controls","unrelated to time"],"slower than expected","This adjective can describe delayed or slowed development.","meaning"),Q("retarded.q2","retarded.s2","register","How should the outdated people-label retarded be used today?",["Avoid it and use respectful current language","Use it as a neutral diagnosis","Use it as a friendly nickname"],"Avoid it and use respectful current language","The source marks the label as insulting and outdated.","register"),Q("retarded.q3","retarded.s1","context","Which sentence uses retarded in the non-person, developmental sense?",["Salt retarded the seedlings' growth.","The nurse called a patient retarded.","The teacher used the word as a nickname."],"Salt retarded the seedlings' growth.","The adjective describes slower plant growth.","context"),Q("retarded.q4","retarded.s2","meaning","A modern report should refer to ___.",["a person with an intellectual disability","a person by an insulting obsolete label","a person's disability as a joke"],"a person with an intellectual disability","Use person-first respectful wording rather than the outdated label.","meaning")]});
D("retch",{etymology:E("From Middle English rechen, of uncertain earlier origin; the verb has long described the movement and sound of trying to vomit.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retch"),contexts:[C("retch.s1","健康","The sharp smell of spoiled fish made the cook retch, although her stomach was empty.","腐鱼的刺鼻气味让厨师干呕，尽管她的胃里是空的。","Retch means make the movement and sound of vomiting without bringing anything up.","Although contrasts the heaving action with an empty stomach.","The cook gags but does not vomit.")],mistakes:[M("confusable","The cook retched a bowl of soup onto the floor after eating it.","The cook vomited a bowl of soup onto the floor after eating it.","Retch means heave as if vomiting without bringing anything up; actual expulsion is vomit.")],quiz:[Q("retch.q1","retch.s1","meaning","Someone who retches makes the movement of vomiting but ___.",["brings nothing up","sings a loud note","answers a survey"],"brings nothing up","Retching is dry heaving without stomach contents coming up.","meaning"),Q("retch.q2","retch.s1","context","A foul odor makes the passenger gag and retch. What is the passenger doing?",["heaving as if about to vomit","writing a job résumé","returning to a seat"],"heaving as if about to vomit","The verb describes the heaving reflex.","context"),Q("retch.q3","retch.s1","confusable","Which verb means actually bring stomach contents up?",["vomit","retch","resound"],"vomit","Retching does not bring anything up; vomiting does.","confusable"),Q("retch.q4","retch.s1","grammar","Choose the sentence using retch correctly.",["The spoiled smell made him retch.","The spoiled smell retched him a bowl.","He retch the spoiled smell yesterday."],"The spoiled smell made him retch.","Make someone retch describes the odor triggering dry heaving.","grammar")]});
D("retell",{etymology:E("Formed from re- ‘again’ + tell, from Old English tellan ‘count, relate’; it means tell a story or report again, sometimes in a new form.","https://www.etymonline.com/word/retell"),contexts:[C("retell.s1","教育","After listening to the recording twice, each student retold the instructions in their own words.","听了两遍录音后，每名学生都用自己的话复述了说明。","Retell means tell a story or information again.","After gives the preparation; in their own words describes the students' phrasing.","The same instructions are repeated in new words.") ,C("retell.s2","文學","The playwright retold the old folktale as a drama set in a modern apartment block.","剧作家把古老民间故事改写成一部以现代公寓楼为背景的戏剧。","Retell can mean tell an old tale again in a new form.","As introduces the new form; set in places the story in a new setting.","The story is adapted rather than merely repeated.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The teacher asked each pupil retell the story using their own words.","The teacher asked each pupil to retell the story using their own words.","Ask someone to do something takes an infinitive with to.")],quiz:[Q("retell.q1","retell.s1","meaning","To retell a news report is to ___.",["tell it again","erase it from memory","sell the newspaper"],"tell it again","The first sense is repeating a story or information.","meaning"),Q("retell.q2","retell.s2","context","A filmmaker retells a myth as a science-fiction story when the filmmaker ___.",["adapts the old tale into a new form","copies a weather report word for word","stops the myth from being known"],"adapts the old tale into a new form","The second sense is a new-form adaptation.","context"),Q("retell.q3","retell.s1","grammar","The guide asked us ____ the route in our own words.",["to retell","retelling","retell to"],"to retell","Ask someone to do something takes the infinitive.","grammar"),Q("retell.q4","retell.s2","meaning","Which example is a creative retelling?",["A folktale is adapted into a play in a new setting.","A student repeats one instruction exactly.","A reporter lists the day's temperature."],"A folktale is adapted into a play in a new setting.","A creative retelling presents an old tale in a new form.","meaning")]});
